<node id="Input Validation Testing">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Input Validation Testing is a domain-focused grouping within the Web Security Testing Guide (WSTG) methodology, explicitly covering testing scenarios related to input validation. It serves as the category for server-side request forgery testing, such as WSTG-INPV-06 and WSTG-INPV-19, as well as other related methodologies. As a core task category, this domain is dedicated to ensuring that all input data is correctly and rigorously validated before being processed by web applications. By focusing on input handling controls, it plays a critical role in preventing attacks that exploit improper data validation, thereby safeguarding business logic and the integrity of data flows within web systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A WSTG category containing test cases related to improper input validation.&lt;SEP&gt;A category within the Web Security Testing Guide that encompasses techniques ensuring user input is properly validated.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-db3753bb1b28c5b9ebe5769dc9c06af2-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1724f5a35cf4fa9478c28ef76ea64632-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1724f5a35cf4fa9478c28ef76ea64632-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-df80c9fe91c3765dc83d86ba6565a823-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ea8988b320818e8e44a6d07527492e35-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-913dbc8a4681245bade3cc137a3a5962-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-913dbc8a4681245bade3cc137a3a5962-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4ddd30d9c938d44180c61ca6f42e47f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffa6824f346bf84b31bce21c39580284-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-06-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-19-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-8-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-10-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-17-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-20-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582831</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reflected Cross Site Scripting">
  <data key="d0">Reflected Cross Site Scripting</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">An injection-based attack that couples scripting code in reflected data to execute in the current user's browser context.&lt;SEP&gt;A web application flaw where user input is echoed unsanitized into HTML pages viewed by others, allowing execution of arbitrary JavaScript.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user input is reflected by the web application without proper encoding, allowing script injection in browsers.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack weakness category where attacker injects executable code into a single HTTP response.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Persistent Cross-Site Scripting">
  <data key="d0">Non-Persistent Cross-Site Scripting</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Subtype of Reflected Cross Site Scripting that targets user-controlled input reflected in responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reflected XSS">
  <data key="d0">Reflected XSS</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Synonym for Reflected Cross Site Scripting used throughout the WSTG content.&lt;SEP&gt;A web application flaw where malicious input is reflected from the server and rendered by the browser leading to script execution or CSS manipulation attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c0346a2efd97b80ae672827b3a9795d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497290</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reflected Search Parameter">
  <data key="d0">Reflected Search Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A parameter within a request URL or form field that reflects back into the HTTP response without proper encoding.&lt;SEP&gt;Target input field source where user-controlled data is directly reflected within query parameters or URLs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User-Controlled HTML Reflected Into Client Route">
  <data key="d0">User-Controlled HTML Reflected Into Client Route</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Target condition where application returns untrusted user input inside HTML responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416447</data>
