<node id="&lt;script&gt; Payload">
  <data key="d0">&lt;script&gt; Payload</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Malicious JavaScript payload commonly used in reflected XSS attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416447</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Browser Executes Injected Script">
  <data key="d0">Browser Executes Injected Script</data>
  <data key="d1">ObservableSignal</data>
  <data key="d2">Evidence observed in the victim browser indicating successful execution of attacker-provided code via a reflected response.&lt;SEP&gt;Evidence of XSS success when victim's browser executes the attacker-provided script code.&lt;SEP&gt;A clear indicator that an injected script has been executed in the client's browser environment, often evidenced by visual changes or message boxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Evidence indicating that malicious code injected into a client-side source executed within the browser DOM or script engine.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd948cd6478c95cb615c3b86568b8163-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd948cd6478c95cb615c3b86568b8163-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-01-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785496787</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JavaScript">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A client-side scripting language commonly reflected during XSS attacks to gain execution capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A scripting language commonly used for injected payloads in Reflected XSS attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The programming language used to manipulate and dynamically generate the DOM structure and behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Client-side scripting language that executes within the browser environment and has access to the DOM and browsing context.&lt;SEP&gt;Client-side scripting language commonly used in web browsers, often targeted by XSS or Flash exploitation techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A prototype-based language where object prototypes and inheritance are dynamically using the prototype chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd948cd6478c95cb615c3b86568b8163-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a331af288c84a3d43384e1ec0cd67904-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0afc271ddfef476dba107d5eebef758e-chunk-002</data>
