<node id="SQL Injection">
  <data key="d0">SQL Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">attacktechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Injection is a well-known weakness class in web applications that occurs when user-supplied input is improperly filtered, sanitized, or validated before being included in SQL database queries. This vulnerability allows attackers to inject malicious SQL code into input fields, which is then interpreted by the database as part of a legitimate query. As a result, the application may execute unauthorized database operations, such as retrieving, modifying, or deleting data, bypassing authentication mechanisms, or escalating privileges. The flaw typically arises when applications concatenate user input directly into dynamic SQL queries without using parameterized queries or proper input validation. This misinterpretation of user input as executable SQL commands enables attackers to manipulate query logic, extract sensitive information, or gain unauthorized access to the database. SQL Injection is a critical security risk within the broader category of injection attacks, and it underscores the importance of secure input handling practices, including input validation, output encoding, and the use of prepared statements. The consequences of such attacks can include data breaches, system compromise, and loss of data integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31756ff9be064b82f25dbfbf1263059b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31756ff9be064b82f25dbfbf1263059b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3057c5214ae12e7effb35fb90f29a423-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d2ff4b7186c17bdc52457e2c1f1dc3fe-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d49f15f997dc4e5a62d377e48dacdb8e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-df80c9fe91c3765dc83d86ba6565a823-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7a6169ed7611988c7689307fbb72ef84-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ea8988b320818e8e44a6d07527492e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a94663073c0acb859206ca0011ed60dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-05-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-apit-99-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athn-04-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athn-11-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-3-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-7-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-8-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-10-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md</data>
