<node id="XML Parser">
  <data key="d0">XML Parser</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The component or system that parses XML input during application processing and is the target of injection testing.&lt;SEP&gt;An XML parsing engine that processes input and validates well-formedness and validation rules.&lt;SEP&gt;The software component responsible for parsing XML and resolving external entity references during document processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Software component responsible for reading, validating, and processing XML documents during application operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The target component that processes the XML input and is vulnerable to injection due to lacking input validation.&lt;SEP&gt;An XML parser component responsible for interpreting and processing XML data sent to a web application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-07-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XML Injection">
  <data key="d0">XML Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where XML data is not properly validated, allowing injection of malicious content into the XML document structure and execution by the parser.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing action that injects specially crafted XML tags, control characters, or entities to subvert input validation and manipulate XML output or application logic.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where injected XML entities alter intended DOM or output behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Introducing crafted XML input to trigger parser behavior that leads to entity resolution or schema-based injection beyond validation.&lt;SEP&gt;An adversarial input containing XML encoding syntax and external entity references that manipulates the target application's processing behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class involving uncontrolled injection of malicious XML tags or structures into an application's processing chain.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5bb2d236b1e2b43118e82283180ff198-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-07-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416532</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Input Data">
  <data key="d0">Input Data</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Data supplied to an XML-consuming endpoint that can include hostile content or testing probes.</data>
