<node id="Command Injection">
  <data key="d0">Command Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">attacktechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Command Injection is a vulnerability class in input validation where user input is passed to an operating system command without proper sanitization, allowing an attacker to inject and execute arbitrary operating system commands on the server. This weakness occurs when untrusted input is executed as system commands, enabling unauthorized code execution. It is a common security flaw in web applications and other software systems that fail to validate or filter user-supplied data before passing it to system shells or command interpreters. Attackers exploit this vulnerability by submitting crafted input—such as through web form fields, URL parameters, or API endpoints—that contains malicious commands. These commands are then executed in the context of the underlying operating system, potentially leading to full system compromise, data theft, or unauthorized actions. Command Injection is a form of injection attack, often used in scenarios where user input is directly embedded into system calls. It is closely related to other injection vulnerabilities, such as SQL injection, but differs in that it targets system-level command execution rather than database queries. The vulnerability arises when applications do not properly escape or validate user input, allowing malicious payloads to be interpreted as executable commands. This weakness class is also referred to as command execution or arbitrary command execution vulnerability. Mitigation strategies include input validation, parameterized commands, sandboxing, and avoiding the use of shell commands with user input. In some cases, the term "Command Injection" may refer to the testing action of sending crafted input to verify the presence of such vulnerabilities, but the primary context remains a security weakness that enables unauthorized system access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a94663073c0acb859206ca0011ed60dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-043536b1d64220258b6e91d8d3fd0aab-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
