<node id="GraphQL Schema">
  <data key="d0">GraphQL Schema</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GraphQL Schema is a structured definition of types, fields, queries, mutations, and relationships that determines what data can be queried or modified in a GraphQL-based API. It serves as the formal model that exposes the API's capabilities to clients by specifying the available object types, fields, enums, arguments, and their connections. Constructed from type definitions, this schema outlines the queryable structure accessible during introspection, thereby revealing all public operations available from the server. In essence, it functions as the concrete artifact that comprehensively defines the entire data model and allowed interactions within the GraphQL API.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-10b0482900b8736b3891a9f801951942-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-366fc7951a16dd549e3f1dc83417fabe-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-366fc7951a16dd549e3f1dc83417fabe-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-006</data>
