<node id="Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is a web security vulnerability class wherein malicious scripts are injected into otherwise benign and trusted websites. These attacks exploit the trust users place in legitimate web applications by injecting malicious client-side code, most commonly JavaScript, into web pages viewed by other users. This code is executed in the user's browser as part of the trusted web page, enabling various malicious outcomes, including credential theft, session hijacking, and malware distribution. XSS typically occurs when web applications improperly validate, sanitize, or encode untrusted user input before reflecting it in web pages, embedding it into HTML templates, or storing it without appropriate protection. The vulnerability manifests through injecting scripts into sinks such as template expressions or raw HTML sections, effectively bypassing input validation mechanisms. While primarily associated with JavaScript injection attacks in typical web contexts, it can have comparable impacts in other technologies, such as similar injection vulnerabilities within Flash contexts identified as XSF. Overall, XSS represents a widespread and severe attack vector that compromises the integrity of web applications and end-user security.&lt;SEP&gt;A client-side injection flaw where malicious scripts are executed inside browsers in the context of a trusted application.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user-supplied input is inserted into a web page without proper sanitization, leading to script execution in the user's browser when pages are loaded.&lt;SEP&gt;A client-side injection technique where malicious scripts are injected into web pages viewed by other users.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack goal to inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users in an effort to steal data or hijack sessions.&lt;SEP&gt;Placement of malicious script into web content which may be used to steal cookies or session tokens</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f4eb0f9a10aea7bceef93114d6569d66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-dd948cd6478c95cb615c3b86568b8163-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c0346a2efd97b80ae672827b3a9795d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6cdc807870a77b5064fef34c66d10a7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-157a4cb1972bdf9a0880f5cf18f04a6a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b26bd7d333a38ea2e920cfcff406e89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-apit-99-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-01-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-05-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-13-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-15-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-04-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583396</data>
