<node id="PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange)">
  <data key="d0">PKCE (Proof Key for Code Exchange)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A protocol extension to OAuth that protects authorization codes without relying on shared secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;A security extension to the Authorization Code flow that enables OAuth on public clients without a secret.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CSRF">
  <data key="d0">CSRF</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Site Request Forgery technique that tricks a user's browser into making unauthorized requests.&lt;SEP&gt;Attackers gain unauthorized access to a user's session via malicious request submission.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Consent Page">
  <data key="d0">Consent Page</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">The user interface displayed to confirm that a Resource Owner consents to client access to a resource.&lt;SEP&gt;User interface presented to the resource owner to request permission for a client to access scopes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="State Parameter">
  <data key="d0">State Parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A unique session token passed during OAuth consent flow to prevent CSRF attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;A unique value generated and stored by the client and sent along with authorization requests to mitigate CSRF attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Anti-CSRF token included in the authorization request to ensure request origin is verified.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-CSRF Request Input Fields">
  <data key="d0">Anti-CSRF Request Input Fields</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Input fields like CSRF tokens used by OAuth flows to prevent cross-site forgery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redirect URL">
  <data key="d0">Redirect URL</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The destination URL the Authorization Server redirects to after session establishment, used in OAuth flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000</data>
