  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Authorization Code">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Authorization Code</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A temporary code exchanged for access tokens, used in the OAuth flow before token issuance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization Code Flow">
  <data key="d0">Authorization Code Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth protocol variant used in the example scenario, specifically focusing on authorization codes and the PKCE extension.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific OAuth 2.0 grant type that exchanges authorization codes for access tokens without revealing credentials to the client.&lt;SEP&gt;A weaker security model or comparative baseline in OAuth flows used for evaluation; tokens are never leaked through the initial response to the client.&lt;SEP&gt;An OAuth grant mechanism combining an authorization code (issued upon user consent) and backend token exchange flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PKCE">
  <data key="d0">PKCE</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Proof Key for Code Exchange extension used to mitigate authorization code interception attacks on public clients.&lt;SEP&gt;Proof Key for Code Exchange; a extension that improves the security of the Authorization Code grant for public clients and confidential ones.&lt;SEP&gt;Proof Key for Code Exchange, a security layer built on the Authorization Code grant that strengthens token issuance, especially for public clients.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Authorization Server">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Authorization Server</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Server component responsible for validating authorization requests, issuing tokens, and controlling access decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The server endpoint responsible for issuing authorization codes, handling token exchanges, and validating user consent.&lt;SEP&gt;Server responsible for managing OAuth authorization flows and granting access tokens to clients.&lt;SEP&gt;A server that issues access tokens and authorization codes based on an OAuth flow.&lt;SEP&gt;The server responsible for validating client credentials and issuing access tokens as part of the OAuth protocol flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Verifier">
  <data key="d0">Code Verifier</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Plaintext input field used to derive the `code_challenge` value in PKCE exchange, reused across multiple requests for a session.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Challenge">
  <data key="d0">Code Challenge</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Hash-based value derived from the code verifier intended to mitigate replay attacks when PKCE is correctly implemented.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Token Exchange">
  <data key="d0">Token Exchange</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Process of submitting the authorization code back to the server along with client credentials and PKCE elements to request an access token.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that exchanges an authorization code or other artifact for a final access token (and optionally a refresh token).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Token Request">
  <data key="d0">Token Request</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The HTTP POST request to the token endpoint containing the authorization code and parameters for exchanging it for an access token.&lt;SEP&gt;HTTP POST request payload containing client credentials, authorization code, and code verification data sent to `/oauth/token` endpoint.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization Server (OAuth)">
  <data key="d0">Authorization Server (OAuth)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A server endpoint that issues authorization codes and grants access tokens to clients via OAuth protocol flows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Authorization Code Flow">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Authorization Code Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The standardized protocol where the client obtains an authorization code from the AS and exchanges it for an access token.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Access Token">
  <data key="d0">Access Token</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A short-lived token issued by the authorization server to access protected resources on behalf of the user.&lt;SEP&gt;A token produced by the authorization server after code exchange, permitting the client to access protected resources on behalf of the user.&lt;SEP&gt;A token issued by the authorization server after successful client authentication, granting permission to invoke protected APIs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bearer-level credential used by the client to access protected resources in place of the user's credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;A credential issued by the Authorization Server that clients present to the Resource Server to request access to protected resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redirect URI Validation Weakness">
  <data key="d0">Redirect URI Validation Weakness</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A flaw where the authorization server accepts an untrusted `redirect_uri` parameter value, allowing redirection to an attacker-controlled location.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client Secret">
  <data key="d0">Client Secret</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A secret shared between the authorization server and a client used to establish trust, protecting token exchange endpoints from unauthorized code injection.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared secret used by the client to authenticate itself to the authorization server during the token request.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Replay">
  <data key="d0">Code Replay</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action that resends an authorization code multiple times, observing if the server associates the same code with multiple token requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494553</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Injection via Confidential Client">
  <data key="d0">Code Injection via Confidential Client</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
