<node id="Clickjacking">
  <data key="d0">Clickjacking</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b26bd7d333a38ea2e920cfcff406e89-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacker possessing client_id can forge consent if consent page (e.g., `/u/consent`) is vulnerable to clickjacking.&lt;SEP&gt;A client-side attack technique that tricks a user into unintentionally interacting with an obscured, fraudulent page while believing they are on the legitimate site.&lt;SEP&gt;A malicious technique where a web user is deceived into interacting with a hidden element on a web page instead of the foreground UI they intend to use.&lt;SEP&gt;Execution of unauthorized actions by tricking a user into clicking on an unintended UI element inside an iframe.&lt;SEP&gt;A UI attack that tricks users into clicking on something different from what they perceive, potentially revealing credentials or approving unintended actions.</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-09-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
