<node id="Cross-Site Scripting">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site Scripting</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d2ff4b7186c17bdc52457e2c1f1dc3fe-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d2">Proper CORS configuration limits access of external resources to prevent XSS from reaching sensitive API endpoints.&lt;SEP&gt;Injection of malicious JavaScript into a cross-site attack context via malformed HTTP response(s) cached and served to legitimate users.</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
