  <data key="d2">Type of Client that cannot protect secret information and is typically associated with frontend applications such as SPAs and mobile apps.&lt;SEP&gt;A client (e.g., frontend/spa/mobile) that cannot securely store credentials and requests access tokens without secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;A client application with limited capabilities to securely store secrets (often in-browser).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Confidential Client">
  <data key="d0">Confidential Client</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d2">Type of Client that can securely protect and use its registration secret (e.g., backend services).&lt;SEP&gt;Type of client that can securely keep authentication secrets and prove its identity to the Authorization Server.&lt;SEP&gt;A client application that stores credentials securely and makes requests on its own behalf (server-side).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resource Server">
  <data key="d0">Resource Server</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The application server that serves the resource content requested by the Client.&lt;SEP&gt;Server that hosts protected resources and validates access tokens issued by the Authorization Server before granting access.&lt;SEP&gt;Target server or endpoint that handles requests protected by access tokens; returns the requested resource if the token is valid.&lt;SEP&gt;The server that exposes protected resources and validates access tokens presented by clients.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth2.0">
  <data key="d0">OAuth2.0</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">An open authorization framework allowing a Client to access protected Resources on behalf of a Resource Owner using tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;An authorization framework allowing clients to access a user's resources on their behalf without sharing credentials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
