  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of client-side XSS where the attacker convinces the user to inject a payload into a web form input, which is then stored in the DOM and reflected in page rendering without proper encoding or escaping.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific client-side vulnerability class that requires the user themselves to inject the payload into an input field for execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aa5c9321922fff53a8b5093aeb86d6b2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-aa5c9321922fff53a8b5093aeb86d6b2-chunk-001</data>
