<node id="Content Security Policy">
  <data key="d0">Content Security Policy</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-aa5c9321922fff53a8b5093aeb86d6b2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-157a4cb1972bdf9a0880f5cf18f04a6a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d2">The CSP may prevent the browser from executing JavaScript within event handlers like onerror.&lt;SEP&gt;A browser-level policy header (CSP) that restricts dynamic resources (e.g., inline scripts, eval usage) from unauthorized origins to mitigate XSS.&lt;SEP&gt;A security policy delivered via HTTP header or meta tag to restrict allowed resources in a web application.&lt;SEP&gt;A server-side HTTP header that defines a whitelist of trusted content sources, enabling browsers to block maliciously injected or cross-site scripting content.</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-01-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-15-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
