</node>
<node id="JavaScript Injection">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A subtype of XSS that allows injection of arbitrary JavaScript code in the browser for execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f4eb0f9a10aea7bceef93114d6569d66-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785496542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="User-Supplied Input">
  <data key="d0">User-Supplied Input</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The data provided by users to the application during requests or interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Untrusted data provided by a user that reaches injection points without proper encoding.&lt;SEP&gt;Data that originates from user input fields (forms, query strings, headers) and is processed by the application.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition that allows any data provided by an end-user to influence server behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Any input field that accepts filenames, paths, or identifiers passed via HTTP request parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;The attacker-provided data entered into web forms, parameters, or inputs that the server later places in HTTP headers without proper sanitization.&lt;SEP&gt;Data provided by the user to web applications that gets placed into server-side templates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f4eb0f9a10aea7bceef93114d6569d66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-507feea21a2b9071c451f23d5f3c743d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4d1e03dc9f13b6dbccbd282894380e7e-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-03-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-04-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-11-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-18-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582790</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JavaScript Execution">
  <data key="d0">JavaScript Execution</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">The strategic objective of executing injected JavaScript within the victim's browser.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f4eb0f9a10aea7bceef93114d6569d66-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785496542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unvalidated Input">
  <data key="d0">Unvalidated Input</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Condition where user-supplied input is not adequately sanitized or validated before use.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where input data is not sufficiently checked for malicious content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f4eb0f9a10aea7bceef93114d6569d66-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d49f15f997dc4e5a62d377e48dacdb8e-chunk-005</data>
