  <data key="d0">CSS Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where user-supplied CSS interferes with legitimate system stylesheets and can enable further attacks such as DOM-based XSS or data exfiltration.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user-supplied CSS code is injected into the application's stylesheet context, potentially allowing malicious behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in web applications where user-controllable input affects CSS rules, allowing data exfiltration, UI manipulation, or attack chaining via style attribute injection or reflected XSS.&lt;SEP&gt;Concrete action of injecting malicious constructs into the CSS context through user input to affect page behavior or extract data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4c0346a2efd97b80ae672827b3a9795d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c0346a2efd97b80ae672827b3a9795d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4c0346a2efd97b80ae672827b3a9795d-chunk-002</data>
