<node id="Content-Security-Policy">
  <data key="d0">Content-Security-Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A HTTP response header that enables a web page administrator to specify which resources the user agent is permitted to load for a particular page.&lt;SEP&gt;A declarative allow-list policy enforced via the `Content-Security-Policy` HTTP header or `&lt;meta&gt;` element to restrict resource origins for scripts, styles, and other resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A declarative allow-list header or meta element restricting which resources such as JavaScript, CSS, images, and files can be loaded in a web application, used as a defense against XSS and clickjacking attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;A header defining a white-list of approved sources from which various content types can be loaded (e.g., scripts, styles).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b26bd7d333a38ea2e920cfcff406e89-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-09-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-conf-12-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-conf-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578983</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="frame-ancestors directive">
  <data key="d0">frame-ancestors directive</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">The part of the CSP header that specifies the restricted source domains allowed to embed content via frames, iframes, objects, or embed tags.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific CSP directive that defines which parent frames are allowed to embed the document, blocking clickjacking attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-09-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anti-CSRF Protection">
  <data key="d0">Anti-CSRF Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">Security mechanisms deployed on web applications to prevent unauthorized commands from cross-site request forgery attacks.</data>
