  <data key="d0">Web Browser</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c2d6cc4252ff2b5d320731c75450c84a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b26bd7d333a38ea2e920cfcff406e89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-94f308342598cce2ab79e26439b43b5f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2df0461e7868bf356c8b0363fdfc1a8b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d2">The user's browser renders the framed content, enabling the clickjacking attack vector.&lt;SEP&gt;A client application interpreting HTTP headers and META tags to enforce security policies for rendering web content.&lt;SEP&gt;Client application where testers can manually probe format string vulnerabilities through user interactions.</data>
