  <data key="d0">Client-side Template Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of attack where user input is inserted into a client-side template engine without proper sanitization or encoding, allowing execution of arbitrary code or data extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;A vulnerability enabling malicious code execution by injecting content into client-side templates.</data>
