<node id="Input Validation Weakness">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation Weakness</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-4fc774259228cd414282425d0a281e37-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-913dbc8a4681245bade3cc137a3a5962-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b6431100fb5694f9e64efa595cebe6c-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d2">A web application vulnerability where objects modified via PATCH lack proper input validation, potentially enabling injection attacks.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in input handling that fails to sanitize or restrict incoming mail protocol commands.&lt;SEP&gt;Gap in validation controls that allows inserted or malformed protocol data to alter how the downstream application interprets and handles the request.</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-06-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-10-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-16-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582541</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
