  <data key="d5">1785578646</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Subdomain Takeover">
  <data key="d0">Subdomain Takeover</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness in DNS management where attacker-owned DNS records claim forgotten or misconfigured subdomains.&lt;SEP&gt;A strategic adversary objective to claim and control a forgotten or abandoned subdomain to host malicious content or redirect traffic.&lt;SEP&gt;The legitimate or illegitimate claim and control of a domain subdomain when the DNS record points to an expired or unclaimed external resource. The goal is to gain ownership for serving malicious content, phishing, session hijacking, credential theft, or full DNS zone control.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-10-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DNS Resource Record">
  <data key="d0">DNS Resource Record</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Entities such as `A`, `CNAME`, `MX`, `NS`, `TXT` used to resolve domain names.&lt;SEP&gt;A DNS record that maps a subdomain name to a specific hostname or IP address for domain resolution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-10-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-existing Resource (Pointed-to Resource)">
  <data key="d0">Non-existing Resource (Pointed-to Resource)</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition where a DNS resource record points to a service, bucket, or route location that no longer exists or is not active.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-10-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578685</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cloud Provider Service (e.g., Azure App Service, AWS S3, GCP Cloud Storage)">
  <data key="d0">Cloud Provider Service (e.g., Azure App Service, AWS S3, GCP Cloud Storage)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A managed service hosted by a cloud provider that can be incorrectly mapped by a DNS record.</data>
