  <data key="d2">A specific directive within a Content Security Policy specifying the allowed base URLs for document elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP directive that defines the base URL that may appear in `&lt;base&gt;` elements or in certain anchor targets within the page to mitigate open redirect or domain spoofing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578910</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="unsafe-inline">
  <data key="d0">unsafe-inline</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A CSP directive value that allows inline JavaScript execution, considered insecure because it relaxes proper source origin checks.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP source value allowing inline script and style execution, significantly weakening XSS protection.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP source value that allows inline execution of scripts or styles, significantly weakening defenses against reflected XSS and other injection attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="unsafe-hashes">
  <data key="d0">unsafe-hashes</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A CSP source value permitting inline execution when provided hashes are predictable or improperly scoped.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP source value that permits loading resources that contain specified hashes; if hashes are weak or inconsistently applied, it can enable unauthorized execution of inline scripts or styles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wildcard Sources">
  <data key="d0">Wildcard Sources</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">Pattern such as `*` or `*.domain.com` in CSP `src` attributes that permits resources from any origin or broad sets of origins, requiring careful validation of allowlisted domains and JSONP endpoints.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Trusted Types">
  <data key="d0">Trusted Types</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A browser technology working alongside Content Security Policy that creates rather restrictive allowlists for trustable values used in dangerous operations such as setting HTML `innerHTML` or using `eval`, reducing DOM-based XSS risks when rigorously enforced.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compliance Requirement">
  <data key="d0">Compliance Requirement</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Organizational obligation or checklist checklist item for merely having a CSP header in place, regardless of its technical effectiveness against real-world attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSONP Route Location">
  <data key="d0">JSONP Route Location</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A designated endpoint on an allowlisted domain that returns JSONP data, commonly discovered when testing partial wildcard sources in Content Security Policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Serialized Object">
  <data key="d0">Serialized Object</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">User-controllable input or server-generated output that contains JSON data or structured serialization often targeted in injection or exposure testing scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="script-src">
  <data key="d0">script-src</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific directive within a Content Security Policy specifying which sources are allowed to serve JavaScript.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Report-Only Content-Security-Policy">
  <data key="d0">Report-Only Content-Security-Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A configuration state where the CSP header is present but set to report-mode only, allowing violations to be logged without blocking malicious content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cryptographically-Random Nonce">
  <data key="d0">Cryptographically-Random Nonce</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A unique, random value (preferably base64-encoded) generated for each HTTP response to validate script sources securely.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strict-Dynamic">
  <data key="d0">Strict-Dynamic</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A CSP directive value that allows script execution only from sources that have been opted-in via nonce or hash for that specific request.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross Site Scripting (XSS)">
  <data key="d0">Cross Site Scripting (XSS)</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A client-side code injection flaw that allows an attacker to inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CSP Validation">
  <data key="d0">CSP Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing action of deploying CSP in Report-Only mode first to observe and validate policy effectiveness before enforcing it.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Inline Script Injection">
  <data key="d0">Inline Script Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing probe involving injecting inline JavaScript code into input fields or user content in order to test CSP enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data URL–based Payloads">
  <data key="d0">Data URL–based Payloads</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Malicious data object URLs embedded in input to bypass CSP restrictions by delivering untrusted data as base64-encoded resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSONP Callback Manipulation">
  <data key="d0">JSONP Callback Manipulation</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A technique using allowlisted JSONP callback endpoints to deliver and execute attacker-controlled JavaScript while respecting CSP source whitelist rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-conf-12-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785578911</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Missing Content-Security-Policy">
  <data key="d0">Missing Content-Security-Policy</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A target condition where no CSP header or meta element is sent, indicating no policy is in place to restrict resource loading origins.</data>
