  <data key="d2">The protocol and transport layer method that used TLS to encrypt and authenticate communications between client and server.&lt;/description&gt;&lt;SEP&gt;Secure network protocol for encrypting data in transit between client and server.&lt;SEP&gt;A protocol that encrypts data in transit to prevent unauthorized access or interception.&lt;SEP&gt;A secure transport protocol that encrypts session data in transit to prevent eavesdropping.&lt;SEP&gt;A network protocol combining HTTP with TLS/SSL for encrypted data transmission.</data>
