<node id="File Include Payload">
  <data key="d0">File Include Payload</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A base64-encoded string containing malicious PHP code that is injected into parameter values for inclusion testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A template parameterized with vulnerable file path placeholders, such as `include/../../config.php`, used to probe for inclusion vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-11-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785581676</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Local File Inclusion">
  <data key="d0">Local File Inclusion</data>
  <data key="d1">vulnerabilityclass</data>
  <data key="d2">Local File Inclusion is a weakness class in software security where an application retrieves or includes local files without proper validation of user-provided file paths. This vulnerability typically arises when user input is directly used to specify file locations, often through directory traversal patterns, allowing attackers to access files beyond the intended scope. The core issue lies in the lack of input sanitization and access control, which enables unauthorized access to sensitive files on the server. Attackers can exploit this weakness to include and read arbitrary local files, potentially exposing configuration files, credentials, or other confidential data. In some cases, the vulnerability may also allow the execution of local files, further escalating the risk to the system. This weakness class is commonly found in applications that dynamically include files based on user input, such as in scripting languages or web applications using server-side includes. The vulnerability stems from insecure input handling and improper validation, making it critical to implement strict path validation, access controls, and input filtering to prevent exploitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-11-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1787991494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Local File Inclusion</data>
</node>
<node id="Remote File Inclusion">
  <data key="d0">Remote File Inclusion</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where an application retrieves files from external URLs without proper validation of user-provided remote paths or root restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-11-1-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785581676</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
