<node id="Incubated Vulnerability">
  <data key="d0">Incubated Vulnerability</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A persistence-based security weakness that requires an initial validation flaw to store malicious data, which can later be retrieved and exploited by the system or users.&lt;SEP&gt;A two-stage attacker-set persistence vulnerability where an operationally useful payload is first injected/stored through a validation flaw, then executed when later accessed by an unsuspecting user.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Data Persistence Layer">
  <data key="d0">Data Persistence Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The server-side component responsible for storing data, often targeted for injecting incubated attack vectors via weak validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unauthorized Data Planting">
  <data key="d0">Unauthorized Data Planting</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action where a malicious payload is stored in the server's persistence layer through a data injection flaw.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582276</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Asynchronous Attack">
  <data key="d0">Asynchronous Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">The strategic objective to attack a large number of victims simultaneously by exploiting one flaw to reach many users at once.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weak Output Validation">
  <data key="d0">Weak Output Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A flaw where data is rendered to the user without proper encoding or neutralization of malicious content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Watering Hole Attack">
  <data key="d0">Watering Hole Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">An attack strategy where trustworthy sites frequented by many users are compromised to deliver malware or steal credentials from subsequent visitors.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unsuspecting User">
  <data key="d0">Unsuspecting User</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d2">The attacker's reusable ability to reach subsequent victims who trust the legitimate site and access the malicious payload.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Corrupted Media Files Upload">
  <data key="d0">Corrupted Media Files Upload</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A malicious file upload action where attackers submit manipulated media files to exploit known vulnerabilities such as CVE-2004-0200 or CVE-2004-0597.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Recall Step">
  <data key="d0">Recall Step</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d2">The attacker-controlled condition or mechanism that triggers exploitation after stored malicious data is recalled by the application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582277</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
