<node id="HTTP Response Headers">
  <data key="d0">HTTP Response Headers</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Response metadata fields that can be manipulated to introduce CRLF sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;The set of HTTP header fields that carry meta-data and are vulnerable to injection when user input flows into their values.&lt;SEP&gt;Components of HTTP responses where attacker input is maliciously inserted using split response techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CR and LF Characters">
  <data key="d0">CR and LF Characters</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific input sequence consisting of carriage return (`\r`) and line feed (`\n`) characters, used to split HTTP responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Browser Web Cache">
  <data key="d0">Browser Web Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">An intermediate system that stores HTTP responses to serve them quickly, potentially storing poisoned responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTTP Response Splitting">
  <data key="d0">HTTP Response Splitting</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where unsanitized user input is reflected into HTTP response headers containing CRLF sequences, allowing multiple responses to be sent in a single request.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing technique that injects CRLF (`%0d%0a`) sequences into HTTP headers to create multiple response blocks, mislead parsers, and manipulate caches or client behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where applications incorporate unsanitized user input directly into HTTP response headers without validating Carriage Return (CR) and Line Feed (LF) characters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Redirection Logic">
  <data key="d0">Redirection Logic</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Server behavior where the destination URL is dynamically set based on user input to redirect the user.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CRLF (%0d%0a)">
  <data key="d0">CRLF (%0d%0a)</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A parameterized, delimiter-based payload containing Carriage Return and Line Feed characters used to inject new header lines in HTTP responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-15-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582324</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Web Cache">
  <data key="d0">Web Cache</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Intermediary storage component that may misinterpret or persist attacker-controlled responses for later request matching.&lt;SEP&gt;A shared or distributed caching layer where manipulated responses can be stored and served to any subsequent authenticating victim.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4ddd30d9c938d44180c61ca6f42e47f-chunk-000</data>
