  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where user input can manipulate object prototypes, allowing attacker-controlled properties to be inherited by unrelated application objects.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class in which user-supplied data mishandles prototype assignment to write into {object prototype}, allowing persistent modification of shared default properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A class of JavaScript injection vulnerability allowing custom properties and methods to be added to core objects via malicious `__proto__` modifications.</data>
