<node id="Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">An attack that tricks a user's browser into making unauthorized requests on their behalf using an authenticated session.&lt;SEP&gt;Attack vector exploiting unintended user actions within web applications using stolen session cookies&lt;SEP&gt;A malicious attack goal where an authenticated user is tricked into submitting unauthorized requests on the application's behalf.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HttpOnly Cookie Attribute">
  <data key="d0">HttpOnly Cookie Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A cookie attribute flag that instructs the browser not to expose the cookie through JavaScript, reducing client-side manipulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cookie attribute that ensures cookies cannot be accessed by client-side scripting languages such as JavaScript&lt;SEP&gt;A flag preventing client-side JavaScript from accessing session cookies, reducing the attack surface for XSS-based session hijacking.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2df0461e7868bf356c8b0363fdfc1a8b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-03-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583420</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secure Cookie Attribute">
  <data key="d0">Secure Cookie Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A cookie attribute flag that instructs the browser to only transmit the cookie over HTTPS connections, preventing interception in transit.&lt;SEP&gt;Security-related cookie attribute used to protect against unauthorized access and tampering&lt;SEP&gt;An optional attribute setting that restricts transmission of a cookie to encrypted HTTPS connections only.&lt;SEP&gt;The `Secure` cookie flag that marks cookies as transmitted only over HTTPS.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2ab4b970856023b5f961a9117891837-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2ab4b970856023b5f961a9117891837-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-09-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785584087</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remember Me Cookie">
  <data key="d0">Remember Me Cookie</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A persistent cookie used to remember user login states beyond the browser session duration without full password reuse.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Weak Cookie Attribute">
  <data key="d0">Weak Cookie Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">ObservableSignal</data>
  <data key="d2">An observable indicator that a cookie lacks proper security attributes or has overly permissive configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Indicative pattern in cookie attributes that suggests insufficient security configuration or missing protection mechanisms</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583396</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SameSite Cookie Attribute">
  <data key="d0">SameSite Cookie Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A cookie attribute configured in three modes to prevent cookies from being sent in cross-site requests and mitigate CSRF.&lt;SEP&gt;A cookie attribute that controls whether cookies are sent with cross-site requests, reducing the effectiveness of CSRF attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-004</data>
