<node id="Session Management">
  <data key="d0">Session Management</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-83827c52b87edd7a3b3969c34753607b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0494a6f833c36d4bb797a335271d7b57-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0494a6f833c36d4bb797a335271d7b57-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d2">The persistent artifact facilitates extended session persistence beyond initial session expiration.&lt;SEP&gt;An area of application security that becomes vulnerable if session state relies solely on client-side information without origin checks.&lt;SEP&gt;Preserving or controlling user session state to maintain authenticated access and authorizations throughout application use.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing domain concerned with the lifecycle, handling, and security of user session identifiers.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing and control domain focused on the creation, maintenance, and termination of user sessions.</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-05-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-08-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-11-methodology.md</data>
