  <data key="d0">Browser-Automatically-Sends-Cookies</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Web browser behavior where it automatically forwards session cookies with subsequent requests to the same origin without explicit user interaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Attacker-Knowledge-Of-Application-URLs">
  <data key="d0">Attacker-Knowledge-Of-Application-URLs</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Attacker's ability to identify valid web application request URLs, form parameters, and legitimate values through analysis or observation of the application's HTML and JavaScript.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authenticated-User-Victim">
  <data key="d0">Authenticated-User-Victim</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">User who has successfully authenticated to a web application and whose browser stores session-related information that can be automatically included in subsequent requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="CSRF-Token">
  <data key="d0">CSRF-Token</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A token value added to requests to ensure they originate from the web application itself, commonly used to mitigate Cross-Site Request Forgery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SameSite-Cookie-Attribute">
  <data key="d0">SameSite-Cookie-Attribute</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A cookie attribute that instructs the browser not to send cookies with cross-origin requests, used to reduce CSRF risk.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Site State Change">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Site State Change</data>
  <data key="d1">ObservableSignal</data>
  <data key="d2">Indicator that the application reflects changes in state initiated by a request, which may confirm unintended action execution in the user's authenticated session.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTML-Image-Tag">
  <data key="d0">HTML-Image-Tag</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-side tag (e.g., `&lt;img&gt;`) that automatically sends a GET request to a specified HTTP(S) resource without requiring explicit user action or confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GET-Request">
  <data key="d0">GET-Request</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">HTTP request method that browsers send automatically when opening a web page or following a link, often lacking user permission checks in vulnerable applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Malicious Third-Party Site">
  <data key="d0">Malicious Third-Party Site</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The attacker-controlled website that hosts the self-submitting form and tricks victims into visiting it.&lt;SEP&gt;A site controlled by the attacker used to host and deliver the CSRF exploit page to victims.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Self-Submitting HTML Form">
  <data key="d0">Self-Submitting HTML Form</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A crafted HTML page containing an embedded form that automatically submits itself upon page load.&lt;SEP&gt;An HTML form configured to automatically submit POST requests when clicked.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON Payload">
  <data key="d0">JSON Payload</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Reusable JSON data structure included within a form submission to bypass input field restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="text/plain Encoding">
  <data key="d0">text/plain Encoding</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A form encoding type required to ensure custom or non-standard payloads are delivered without modification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583536</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidden Input Field">
  <data key="d0">Hidden Input Field</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action that includes hidden fields in an HTML form to silently transmit malicious parameters alongside legitimate ones.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authenticated User Session">
  <data key="d0">Authenticated User Session</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Active session identified by session cookie indicating logged-in state.&lt;SEP&gt;A session identifier stored on the client or server-side that authenticates the user across requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross Site Request Forgery">
  <data key="d0">Cross Site Request Forgery</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness in session management where an attacker can induce a user's browser to send unintended requests to a web application.&lt;SEP&gt;An attack that forces the victim's browser to perform unintended state-altering operations on an authenticated web application.&lt;SEP&gt;Unauthorized modification of the victim's session by tricking the web application into processing unauthorized requests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Client-Side Session Management">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Session Management</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Session management relying exclusively on values available to the browser such as cookies and HTTP authentication credentials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="JSON-Payload Form">
  <data key="d0">JSON-Payload Form</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A form POST payload delivered as plain text using `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` encoding with a JSON string inside a hidden input field.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Padded Input Field">
  <data key="d0">Padded Input Field</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">An extra input field in the form submission used to evade known input whitelist or validation rules.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hidden Input Element">
  <data key="d0">Hidden Input Element</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">HTML form component used to embed request parameters that are not visible to standard users but are submitted with the form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Browser HTTP Request">
  <data key="d0">Browser HTTP Request</data>
  <data key="d1">ObservableSignal</data>
  <data key="d2">The HTTP request actually transmitted by the victim's browser following the JavaScript form submission.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Script Auto-Submission">
  <data key="d0">Script Auto-Submission</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A JavaScript command (often `onload`, `submit()` on form element) that automatically triggers form submission without user action.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="History Push State">
  <data key="d0">History Push State</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A JavaScript method (`history.pushState()`) used to modify the browser URL to avoid typical page reload detection mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583537</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HTML Image Tag (`img`)">
  <data key="d0">HTML Image Tag (`img`)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard HTML element whose `src` attribute triggers automatic browser requests regardless of content legitimacy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-005</data>
