<node id="Source Code Review">
  <data key="d0">Source Code Review</data>
  <data key="d1">defensivecontrol</data>
  <data key="d2">Source Code Review is a security testing action that involves examining the source code of an application to identify vulnerabilities, sensitive information, or security weaknesses. This process is typically conducted as part of a broader security assessment to detect flaws such as Local File Inclusion, Credential Exposure, or other exploitable conditions. It may also involve the retrieval and analysis of source code to uncover secrets, sensitive data, or unintended execution paths. The primary objectives include detecting and mitigating security risks, ensuring secure coding practices, and identifying potential attack vectors. Source Code Review can be performed manually or through automated tools and is often used to verify the integrity and security of software before deployment. The technique is employed both as a proactive measure to improve code quality and as a reactive method to address known or suspected vulnerabilities. While it is commonly categorized as a testing action, it may also be leveraged in attack scenarios to exploit weaknesses in application logic or data handling. Overall, Source Code Review plays a critical role in enhancing software security by enabling the discovery and remediation of flaws at the code level.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-83827c52b87edd7a3b3969c34753607b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-08-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-429f1cea7765f3e2.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4c91a7e4da4eea3a.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-2e266fadcba1fc0d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f43f768c997245d2.md</data>
