<node id="Accessible SMB Share">
  <data key="d0">Accessible SMB Share</data>
  <data key="d1">preconditionenvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A target condition where an SMB share is accessible and can be used for authentication or data access.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where an SMB share is accessible.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where an SMB share is accessible to the attacker.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where an SMB share is accessible for network access.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where a Server Message Block share is reachable from the attacker's position.&lt;SEP&gt;A target condition where an SMB share is accessible and can be read or written to.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-043536b1d64220258b6e91d8d3fd0aab-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ef35e26658bdcdb6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1787996825</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Accessible SMB Share</data>
</node>
<node id="LDAP-Backed Query Path">
  <data key="d0">LDAP-Backed Query Path</data>
  <data key="d1">preconditionenvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">LDAP-Backed Query Path is a target condition in which query paths rely on the Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP) for authentication, data retrieval, or authorization processes. These query paths involve the use of LDAP as a backend system, where queries are processed through LDAP services or routed through LDAP infrastructure. The reliance on LDAP enables certain attack vectors, including LDAP injection, manipulation, and exploitation of authentication paths. In some cases, LDAP queries are used to retrieve data, potentially exposing sensitive information or enabling unauthorized access. This condition is particularly relevant in environments where query logic depends on LDAP for authentication or lookup operations, making it a potential entry point for security testing and exploitation. The use of LDAP in query processing can create attack paths that are leveraged for penetration testing or malicious activities, especially when input validation is inadequate. Overall, LDAP-Backed Query Path represents a scenario where the integration of LDAP into query workflows introduces both functional capabilities and security risks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-3002b69a47310ca1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7ff057962935cb60.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-938bc49bb5da258f.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1787996761</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">LDAP-Backed Query Path</data>
</node>
<node id="Writable WebDAV Path">
  <data key="d0">Writable WebDAV Path</data>
  <data key="d1">preconditionenvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Writable WebDAV Path is a target condition indicating that a specific WebDAV path is writable and accessible, allowing for file upload and manipulation. This condition typically arises when a WebDAV endpoint permits write access, enabling the creation, modification, or deletion of files on the server. The path must be both writable and reachable, often through standard WebDAV protocols such as HTTP or HTTPS. In security contexts, this condition is particularly significant when an attacker can exploit the writable path to upload malicious files, execute code, or alter existing content. The ability to manipulate files via the WebDAV path may be leveraged for persistent access, data exfiltration, or lateral movement within a network. The condition may also be associated with misconfigured server settings or insufficient access controls, where write permissions are granted without proper authentication or authorization. In some cases, the writable path is specifically exploitable by an attacker, making it a critical vulnerability in web application and server security assessments. The presence of a writable WebDAV path can facilitate various attack vectors, including web shell deployment or privilege escalation, depending on the server's configuration and the permissions granted to the user or service account.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-043536b1d64220258b6e91d8d3fd0aab-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3002b69a47310ca1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4c91a7e4da4eea3a.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-463bc40b9d3a7e65.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-045067d746e8d66c.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ef35e26658bdcdb6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f43f768c997245d2.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1787996755</data>
