  <data key="d7">Writable WebDAV Path</data>
</node>
<node id="Boolean Response Difference">
  <data key="d0">Boolean Response Difference</data>
  <data key="d1">preconditionenvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Boolean Response Difference is a target condition characterized by variations in system responses based on input, particularly when those responses differ in boolean form (e.g., true/false) depending on the evaluation of a condition or input. This phenomenon occurs when the system's output changes in response to different inputs or states, indicating that the underlying logic is sensitive to boolean evaluations. Such differences can reveal conditional behavior, enabling inference about internal logic or system state. In many cases, the variation in responses—such as a shift from true to false or vice versa—suggests a change in application behavior or the presence or absence of a resource or state. These discrepancies may also point to potential misconfigurations, logic flaws, or vulnerabilities, as inconsistent responses can be exploited to infer system internals or trigger unintended behavior. The condition is frequently observed in security contexts, where differing responses based on boolean logic can indicate possible exploitability or vulnerabilities. It is also useful for detection and analysis, as variations in responses based on input or boolean conditions allow for the identification of logic-based behavior and potential weaknesses in system design. Overall, Boolean Response Difference serves as both an indicator of conditional processing and a potential signal for further investigation into system integrity, logic correctness, or security posture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-043536b1d64220258b6e91d8d3fd0aab-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-00