<node id="Weak Or Reused Password Exists">
  <data key="d0">Weak Or Reused Password Exists</data>
  <data key="d1">preconditionenvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Weak Or Reused Password Exists is a target condition indicating the presence of passwords in a system that are either weak—such as being easily guessable due to simplicity or common usage—or reused across multiple accounts or systems. This condition represents a significant security vulnerability, as weak passwords can be rapidly cracked using automated tools like brute-force or dictionary attacks. Similarly, reused passwords increase risk because compromising one account can lead to unauthorized access to other accounts that share the same credentials. The presence of such passwords enables credential-based attacks, including password spraying and credential stuffing, which exploit predictable or shared login information. This condition elevates the overall risk of unauthorized access and data breaches, as attackers can leverage compromised credentials to gain entry into systems without requiring additional exploitation techniques. The persistence of weak or reused passwords across systems underscores a critical gap in authentication security practices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7ff057962935cb60.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-938bc49bb5da258f.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-463bc40b9d3a7e65.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67281ef7361eaa1e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-db59b660c03f0d7d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-a9ccf5fa80acec79.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md</data>
