<node id="Coerced SMB Authentication">
  <data key="d0">Coerced SMB Authentication</data>
  <data key="d1">attacktechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action that forces an SMB authentication attempt by the target system.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that forces a target system to authenticate to an attacker-controlled SMB server.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that coerces the target to authenticate to an attacker-controlled SMB server.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that forces a target system to authenticate to an attacker-controlled server over SMB.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that forces an SMB authentication attempt from a target system.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that forces the target to authenticate to an attacker-controlled SMB server.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that forces authentication to an SMB share by exploiting a server-side URL fetch feature.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1787996751</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Coerced SMB Authentication</data>
</node>
<node id="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d0">Offline Password Cracking</data>
  <data key="d1">attacktechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Offline Password Cracking is an action or attack technique that involves the offline processing of captured password hashes or credentials to recover plaintext passwords and obtain user credentials. This process typically uses tools and wordlists to systematically attempt to crack the hashes, often leveraging computational resources to test potential password combinations. The primary goal is to extract valid credentials from hashed data, which may have been obtained through various means such as system breaches, network sniffing, or compromised databases. Offline Password Cracking can be employed in both malicious and ethical contexts: as a cyberattack to gain unauthorized access to user accounts or systems, or as a security testing action to assess the strength of password storage mechanisms and identify vulnerabilities in authentication systems. The technique relies on the assumption that password hashes—especially those stored without proper salting or encryption—can be reverse-engineered through brute force, dictionary attacks, or rainbow table methods. It is commonly used in penetration testing to evaluate password resilience and to ensure that systems enforce strong password policies. The process may involve extracting hash data from system files, memory dumps, or network captures, followed by offline analysis using specialized software. While the method does not require real-time interaction with target systems, it demands significant computational power and time, especially when dealing with complex or well-protected hashes. Ultimately, Offline Password Cracking highlights the importance of secure password hashing practices, such as using salted and iterated hashing algorithms, to mitigate the risk of credential compromise.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-00