  <data key="d7">WinRM Credential Login</data>
</node>
<node id="Executable Upload Webshell">
  <data key="d0">Executable Upload Webshell</data>
  <data key="d1">attacktechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">Executable Upload Webshell is an action or technique involving the upload of an executable file—often a malicious script or payload—to a web server or target system with the intent of establishing a webshell. This webshell serves as a backdoor, enabling remote access, arbitrary code execution, and persistent control over the compromised system. The uploaded executable is typically designed to be executed through a web interface, allowing attackers to interact with the target system via HTTP requests. This method is commonly used in cyberattacks to gain unauthorized access, maintain persistence, and execute commands remotely. The process may involve exploiting vulnerabilities in web applications, misconfigured file upload functionalities, or weak authentication mechanisms. While primarily associated with malicious intent, the same technique can be used in ethical hacking or penetration testing scenarios to assess system vulnerabilities and validate security controls. In such contexts, the upload is conducted legally and with proper authorization to evaluate the effectiveness of defenses. The executable may be disguised with benign file extensions or obfuscated to evade detection by security tools. Ultimately, the goal of an Executable Upload Webshell is to establish a foothold on the target system, enabling further exploitation, data exfiltration, or lateral movement within a network.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-00