<node id="Database Dump">
  <data key="d0">Database Dump</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Database Dump is a concrete artifact or object that contains a full or partial export, copy, or dump of a database's contents, typically obtained during an attack or from a target system. It represents a structured data extraction, often involving sensitive information, and may be produced through methods such as file read operations or database injection. The dump can be a complete or partial representation of the database, including both raw and processed data, and is frequently used for analysis, forensic examination, or malicious purposes. As a concrete database export artifact, it is commonly obtained from the target system and may exist in various file formats. The term is often used interchangeably with terms such as database export, data dump, or database extraction, and is frequently associated with cybersecurity incidents where unauthorized access leads to the acquisition of sensitive data.</data>
