<node id="JWT Secret Weakness">
  <data key="d0">JWT Secret Weakness</data>
  <data key="d1">vulnerabilityclass</data>
  <data key="d2">JWT Secret Weakness is a vulnerability class involving the insecure handling, exposure, or weakness of JSON Web Token (JWT) signing secrets. This weakness arises when the secret used to sign JWTs is weak, predictable, or improperly protected, making it susceptible to compromise. When the secret is weak—such as being easily guessed or derived—or exposed through insecure storage, configuration errors, or code leaks, attackers can forge valid tokens. This enables unauthorized access to systems or data, as forged tokens can be accepted as legitimate by the authentication system. The issue may also stem from poor management practices, such as using default secrets, hardcoding secrets in source code, or failing to rotate secrets regularly. Predictable secrets, including those based on common patterns or insufficient entropy, further increase the risk of token forgery. In some cases, the exposure of the secret may occur through logging, version control systems, or insecure APIs. The consequences of this weakness include session hijacking, privilege escalation, and unauthorized data access. The vulnerability is not limited to a single scenario but can manifest across various applications that rely on JWTs for authentication and authorization. Mitigation strategies include using strong, randomly generated secrets, securely storing them (e.g., via environment variables or secret management tools), rotating them periodically, and ensuring that secrets are never embedded in client-side code or logs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-d1ffa3e33fee59c7.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7ff057962935cb60.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4c91a7e4da4eea3a.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-938bc49bb5da258f.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-463bc40b9d3a7e65.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-045067d746e8d66c.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-b5628ce0b17f7e70.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f43f768c997245d2.md</data>
