<edge source="Path Traversal" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Path Traversal-SQL Injection File Read is a technique that exploits the path traversal vulnerability class to gain unauthorized access to files on a system. This technique leverages the path traversal weakness, which allows an attacker to manipulate file paths to access files outside the intended directory. The method is used to test or exploit path traversal vulnerabilities, often in conjunction with SQL injection to read sensitive files. It supports path traversal as a vulnerability class and is specifically designed to exploit the path traversal weakness. The technique is employed to access files that should be restricted, potentially leading to data exposure. The vulnerability class is exploited by this technique, which enables attackers to read files through manipulated input, highlighting the interplay between path traversal and SQL injection in file access attacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, exploits, tests or exploits</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67281ef7361eaa1e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md</data>
  <data key="d13">1787992327</data>
