<edge source="PHP" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d8">16.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (Offline Password Cracking, PHP) refers to a technique that involves the use of PHP as a core component within the technology stack. This technique is specifically designed to target PHP-based applications and environments, leveraging the PHP programming language and its associated frameworks. It is relevant to systems built on the PHP technology stack and often utilizes PHP scripts or tools to perform offline password cracking operations. The method relies on PHP's capabilities to execute server-side logic, making it applicable in scenarios where PHP applications are deployed in web environments. This includes analyzing PHP-generated authentication mechanisms, parsing PHP code for vulnerabilities, or exploiting weaknesses in PHP-based password handling routines. The technique is particularly effective in environments where PHP is used for backend processing, such as content management systems, e-commerce platforms, or custom web applications. It may involve reverse engineering PHP scripts, extracting password hashes, or using PHP-based tools to perform brute-force or dictionary attacks offline. The reliance on PHP as a technology stack implies that the technique is most applicable in systems where PHP is the primary language for server-side scripting.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique is relevant to the PHP technology stack.&lt;SEP&gt;The PHP technology stack supports the offline password cracking technique.</data>
