<edge source="Command Output" target="SSRF Localhost Probing">
  <data key="d8">15.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Command Output-SSRF Localhost Probing refers to a technique used in security testing where the command output serves as a signal indicating the success of a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attack targeting localhost. The command output can indicate the result of the technique, often reflecting whether the attack successfully accessed internal resources or services on the target system. This output may include data retrieved from localhost, such as file contents, internal API responses, or error messages, which confirm that the SSRF attack was successful. The technique relies on the command output as a measurable indicator of success, with the output itself being a direct result of the attack’s execution. In some cases, the command output may also reveal the internal state of the system, such as the presence of specific services or configurations, further validating the attack's effectiveness. The success of the technique is often confirmed through the presence of specific patterns or content in the command output, which can be analyzed to determine whether the probing was successful. Command output can thus be used both as a confirmation of the attack’s success and as a source of information about the internal system. The technique can produce command output as a signal, and this output is frequently used in security assessments to verify the existence of SSRF vulnerabilities. The command output may indicate successful command execution, which is a key indicator that the SSRF attack was able to interact with internal network resources. Overall, the command output is a critical component in assessing the success of SSRF localhost probing, providing tangible evidence of the attack's impact.</data>
  <data key="d10">produces, indicates, indicated by</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000</data>
