<edge source="Credentials" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">14.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation Credentials-SQL Injection File Read refers to a technique that enables the extraction of credentials through SQL injection vulnerabilities, often by exploiting misconfigurations or insecure database queries. This method can result in the production of a credentials artifact, which is a digital file or data structure containing sensitive authentication information such as usernames, passwords, or access tokens. The technique may be used to read files from the database server or the underlying file system, potentially revealing stored credentials. The output of this process is consistently described as producing credentials or a credentials artifact, indicating that the primary outcome is the acquisition of authentication data. The term "credentials artifact" is used interchangeably with "credentials" in the descriptions, suggesting that the result is a structured representation of sensitive login information, possibly stored in a file or log. The technique is primarily associated with cybersecurity contexts, particularly in penetration testing and threat modeling, where it is leveraged to assess system vulnerabilities. While the descriptions vary slightly in phrasing, they all converge on the same core function: the generation of credentials through SQL injection, potentially via file read operations. There are no conflicting interpretations across the descriptions; all emphasize the production of credentials as an outcome, with minor variations in terminology regarding the format or classification of the output.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique can produce credentials as an artifact.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique can produce a credentials artifact.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique produces credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique can produce the credentials artifact.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique can produce credentials artifact.</data>
  <data key="d10">can produce,produced,produces</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
