<edge source="Source Code Review" target="Linux Host">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The technique known as Linux Host-Source Code Review is a method focused on analyzing and evaluating source code within the context of Linux host environments. It specifically targets Linux host systems, utilizing the Linux Host as both a technology stack and a primary operational environment. The approach is relevant to the Linux Host technology stack, emphasizing the importance of understanding and assessing code in relation to this platform. The technique employs the Linux Host as the target technology, indicating that its application is centered on systems operating within this environment. Additionally, Source Code Review is directly associated with the Linux Host technology stack, highlighting the integration of code analysis practices within the broader framework of Linux-based host systems. This method is designed to ensure the quality, security, and functionality of software developed for or running on Linux hosts.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, is relevant to, relevant to</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-001</data>
