<edge source="Source Code Review" target="Boolean Response Delta">
  <data key="d8">9.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Boolean Response Delta-Source Code Review refers to a technique that generates a boolean response delta signal, which is a binary output used to indicate specific outcomes related to the evaluation of source code. This technique produces a boolean response delta, a signal that can convey whether a particular operation or analysis has succeeded or failed. The boolean response delta serves as a diagnostic indicator, reflecting the success of the technique itself. In the context of source code review, this delta can signal the success of the review process, indicating whether the analysis has been completed effectively or if any issues have been identified. Additionally, the boolean response delta may also highlight the presence of vulnerabilities within the source code, thereby providing a direct indication of potential security flaws. As such, the boolean response delta functions both as a measure of the technique's operational success and as a marker for critical findings in code evaluation. The signal's binary nature allows for clear, unambiguous communication of results, making it a valuable component in automated code analysis systems.</data>
  <data key="d10">produces, indicated by, generates</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
