<edge source="User-Controlled Input Reaches Query" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (SQL Injection File Read, User-Controlled Input Reaches Query) describes a security vulnerability condition in which user-controlled input directly reaches a database query. This occurs when data provided by a user is incorporated into a SQL query without proper validation or sanitization, allowing the input to be interpreted as part of the query syntax. The presence of this condition is a prerequisite for certain types of SQL injection attacks, particularly those that enable unauthorized access to or manipulation of database contents. The technique is applicable whenever user input is passed to a query in an untrusted manner, regardless of whether the input is explicitly labeled as "user-controlled" or simply "user input." Multiple descriptions emphasize the importance of the input reaching the query as the core condition, highlighting that the vulnerability arises from the flow of untrusted data into the query execution context. This relation is critical in the context of web application security, as it represents a common vector for attackers to exploit database systems.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies when,is applicable when</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001</data>
