<edge source="User-Controlled Input Reaches Query" target="JWT Token Forgery">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">(JWT Token Forgery, User-Controlled Input Reaches Query) is a technique applicable when user-controlled input reaches a query. This condition arises in systems where input provided by a user is directly incorporated into a query without sufficient validation or sanitization. The presence of this condition is a critical prerequisite for the technique to be effective, as it enables the manipulation of query behavior through crafted user input. The technique leverages this pathway to potentially exploit vulnerabilities, such as those involving JWT token forgery, by influencing the query logic or structure. The consistency across multiple descriptions indicates that the core requirement is the unvalidated passage of user-controlled data into a query context, which may lead to security risks if not properly mitigated. The technique's applicability is strictly dependent on this environmental precondition, highlighting the importance of secure input handling in preventing such exploits.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique is applicable when user-controlled input reaches a query.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique is applicable when user-controlled input reaches a query.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique applies when user-controlled input reaches a query.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies when,is applicable when</data>
