<edge source="Python Web Stack" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Offline Password Cracking-Python Web Stack is a technique that is specifically relevant to the Python Web Stack, a technology stack commonly used for developing web applications using Python-based frameworks. The technique targets the Python Web Stack, leveraging its architecture and components to perform offline password cracking. It is applicable in environments where the Python Web Stack is present, and it utilizes the stack as the primary target technology. The Python Web Stack supports this technique, indicating that certain aspects of its implementation, such as authentication mechanisms or data handling, may be exploitable in an offline context. The relevance of this technique to the Python Web Stack is consistently emphasized across multiple descriptions, highlighting its dependence on the stack’s structure and functionality. This relationship underscores the importance of securing Python-based web applications against such attacks, particularly when password storage or verification processes are not adequately protected.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, relevant to, is relevant to, uses, targets, applies when</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-001</data>
