<edge source="Python Web Stack" target="Executable Upload Webshell">
  <data key="d8">10.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Executable Upload Webshell-Python Web Stack is a technique that leverages the Python Web Stack as a target environment. The Python Web Stack, a technology stack commonly used for developing web applications, supports the execution of the executable upload webshell technique. This technique involves uploading malicious executable files to web applications built on the Python Web Stack, enabling unauthorized access or control over the system. The technique is specifically relevant to applications utilizing the Python Web Stack, as it exploits vulnerabilities within this environment. It uses the Python Web Stack as part of its operational context and targets web applications developed using this technology stack. The technique is closely associated with the Python Web Stack, relying on its architecture and components to execute the webshell payload. The Python Web Stack's support for dynamic content and server-side processing makes it a viable target for such attacks. The technique is applicable to environments where Python-based web frameworks and tools are deployed, highlighting the importance of securing such systems against executable upload vulnerabilities.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, is relevant to, relevant to, uses, targets</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
