<edge source="Python Web Stack" target="JWT Token Forgery">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">JWT Token Forgery-Python Web Stack is a technique that specifically targets applications built on the Python Web Stack, a technology stack commonly used for developing web applications in Python. This technique is relevant to environments where Python-based web frameworks—such as Django, Flask, or FastAPI—are employed, and where JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) are used for authentication and authorization. The method exploits vulnerabilities related to JWT handling within the Python Web Stack, potentially allowing an attacker to forge or manipulate tokens to gain unauthorized access. The technique leverages the architecture and implementation practices of Python web applications, focusing on weaknesses in token validation, signing algorithms, or key management. It is applicable to any system utilizing the Python Web Stack where JWTs are employed, and it is particularly effective when security measures are improperly configured or implemented. The technique is directly tied to the Python Web Stack, making it a critical concern for developers and security professionals working within this technology ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d10">is relevant to, relevant to, uses, targets, applies when</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
