<edge source="Windows Active Directory" target="Executable Upload Webshell">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Executable Upload Webshell-Windows Active Directory is a cyberattack technique that leverages the Windows Active Directory (AD) technology stack as its operational environment. This technique involves the upload of executable files to a compromised system, typically through a webshell, which is then used to establish persistent access or execute malicious commands within the network. The method specifically targets Windows Active Directory environments, exploiting the infrastructure and services provided by AD to maintain stealth and elevate privileges. As part of the broader attack chain, it relies on the integration of AD components such as domain controllers, group policies, and authentication mechanisms. The technique is relevant to the Windows Active Directory technology stack, indicating its dependence on AD's architecture for execution and lateral movement. It is commonly employed in scenarios where attackers aim to exploit trusted network components and maintain control over enterprise environments that rely on AD for identity and access management.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, relevant to, is relevant to</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-001</data>
