<edge source="Windows Active Directory" target="WinRM Credential Login">
  <data key="d8">9.0</data>
  <data key="d9">WinRM Credential Login is a technique relevant to the Windows Active Directory technology stack. It leverages Windows Active Directory as a core component in the authentication process, targeting Windows Active Directory environments and authentication mechanisms. The technique utilizes the Windows Active Directory technology to facilitate credential-based access, often exploiting its integration with Windows systems. It is specifically designed to interact with Windows Active Directory infrastructure, enabling authentication and access control through WinRM (Windows Remote Management) protocols. This method is commonly used in environments where Windows Active Directory serves as the primary identity and access management system. The technique's reliance on Windows Active Directory highlights its focus on leveraging existing directory services for credential validation and remote system access.</data>
  <data key="d10">is relevant to,relevant to,targets,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-001</data>
