<edge source="Container" target="Executable Upload Webshell">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Container-Executable Upload Webshell is a technique that leverages container technology as part of its operational environment. It is specifically designed to target containerized environments and is relevant to the container technology stack. The technique utilizes a container environment to execute malicious activities, with the core mechanism involving the upload of an executable file to a webshell within the container. This approach relies on the container technology stack to support the execution and persistence of the webshell. The technique is closely tied to container technology, both in its implementation and in its operational context, making it applicable in environments where containers are deployed. It operates within the broader framework of container-based systems, exploiting their architecture and runtime behavior to achieve its objectives. The technique's reliance on container technology underscores its relevance to modern cloud-native and containerized application environments.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, relevant to, is relevant to, uses, targets</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000</data>
