<edge source="Container" target="Offline Password Cracking">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The (Container, Offline Password Cracking) relation refers to a technique that leverages container technology for the purpose of offline password cracking. This technique is applicable in environments where container technology is present, utilizing a container environment to perform the cracking process. It targets containers and operates within the broader container technology stack, which supports the execution of offline password cracking. The technique uses container technology and a container environment to facilitate the cracking, with the container environment serving as the operational platform for the process. The relationship highlights the integration of container-based systems into security testing methodologies, particularly in scenarios where password cracking is conducted offline.</data>
