<edge source="Offline Password Cracking" target="Privilege Escalation Path">
  <data key="d8">22.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Offline Password Cracking-Privilege Escalation Path is a technique that enables an attacker to achieve privilege escalation by exploiting offline password cracking methods. This technique requires a privilege escalation path, which refers to a sequence of actions or conditions that allow an attacker to move from a lower-privileged account to a higher-privileged one. The technique supports the establishment of the attacker’s capability to create or exploit such a path, enabling the execution of privilege escalation. It can be used to test for existing privilege escalation paths and to establish the attacker's capability to leverage them. Offline Password Cracking specifically facilitates privilege escalation through the use of cracked credentials, allowing an attacker to gain unauthorized access to systems or accounts with elevated privileges. The technique supports the development of an attacker capability centered on privilege escalation paths, and it enables the creation or utilization of such paths as part of a broader attack strategy. The technique is designed to support the exploitation of vulnerabilities in authentication mechanisms, particularly when password hashes are obtained and processed offline. This capability is essential for adversaries seeking to escalate privileges without direct interaction with the target system in real time.</data>
  <data key="d10">requires, supports, establishes, supports testing for, enables, can establish</data>
