<edge source="Offline Password Cracking" target="Wildcard Command Filter Bypass">
  <data key="d8">15.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Offline Password Cracking-Wildcard Command Filter Bypass is a payload pattern utilized within the context of offline password cracking techniques. This payload is specifically designed to bypass wildcard command filters, enabling attackers to execute malicious commands in environments where such filters are enforced. The payload pattern is integral to the offline password cracking process, as it facilitates the exploitation of command-line interfaces or scripting environments that are vulnerable to wildcard-based input sanitization flaws. It is employed by various offline password cracking tools and methods to circumvent security controls that restrict or filter the use of wildcard characters in command execution. The technique leverages this payload to gain unauthorized access to password hashes or to manipulate password recovery processes, particularly in systems where offline cracking is performed on captured authentication data. The payload pattern is consistently used across multiple implementations of the technique, indicating its established role in bypassing security mechanisms. While the payload is primarily associated with offline password cracking, its functionality is tied to command filter evasion, making it a critical component in scenarios involving privilege escalation or unauthorized access through compromised systems. The use of this payload pattern underscores the importance of robust input validation and secure command execution practices in mitigating such attacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, uses, used by, targets, used in</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3002b69a47310ca1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-d1ffa3e33fee59c7.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-938bc49bb5da258f.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-463bc40b9d3a7e65.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-045067d746e8d66c.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-a9ccf5fa80acec79.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md</data>
