<edge source="WinRM Credential Login" target="Move Laterally">
  <data key="d8">14.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Move Laterally-WinRM Credential Login is a technique that supports the goal of moving laterally within a network. This method enables an attacker to leverage WinRM (Windows Remote Management) credential login to gain access to additional systems, thereby facilitating lateral movement across the network. The technique is specifically designed to achieve the attack objective of expanding access beyond an initial compromised system. It can be used to test for the feasibility of lateral movement by exploiting valid credentials through WinRM. The approach supports both the execution and verification of lateral movement capabilities, allowing an adversary to traverse network segments and access resources on other machines. This technique is particularly effective in environments where WinRM is enabled and credentials are reused across systems. The consistent emphasis across descriptions is on the technique’s role in achieving lateral movement, highlighting its utility in both offensive operations and security testing.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, can support, supports testing for, supports attack goal, supports achieving</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-001</data>
