<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Linux Host">
  <data key="d8">11.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Executable Upload Webshell-Linux Host refers to a cybersecurity technique in which an executable file is uploaded to a Linux host system, typically via a webshell, to gain unauthorized access or execute malicious commands. This technique leverages the Linux host as a critical component of its operational environment, relying on the underlying Linux host technology stack for execution and persistence. The Linux host serves both as the target and the platform upon which the webshell operates, making it essential to the success of the attack. The technique is specifically relevant to Linux host environments, where it exploits vulnerabilities in web applications or misconfigured systems to deploy and run malicious payloads. The use of a Linux host in this context is not incidental but integral, as the operating system's architecture, file system, and command-line interface enable the execution and control of the uploaded webshell. This method is commonly employed in adversarial scenarios where attackers seek to maintain long-term access to a compromised system. The technique’s effectiveness is closely tied to the configuration and security posture of the Linux host, including permissions, network access, and service availability. Overall, the relationship between the executable upload webshell and the Linux host underscores the importance of securing Linux-based systems against webshell-based attacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, is relevant to, supports</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d12">source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4c91a7e4da4eea3a.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md</data>
