<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Privilege Escalation Path">
  <data key="d8">22.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Executable Upload Webshell-Privilege Escalation Path is a cybersecurity technique that facilitates the establishment of a privilege escalation path on a target system. This technique enables the execution of an uploaded webshell, which serves as a foothold for further exploitation. It requires the attacker to possess the capability to escalate privileges, either by leveraging existing vulnerabilities or by creating conditions that allow for such escalation. The technique supports the testing of privilege escalation paths and can establish a privilege escalation path capability on the target system. It is designed to enable the attacker to achieve elevated privileges through the use of a webshell, which may be uploaded via various means, including exploiting insecure file upload functionalities. The technique also requires a privilege escalation path capability, which may involve the ability to execute arbitrary code, gain access to system-level functions, or bypass security controls. In some contexts, the technique is described as enabling privilege escalation paths, indicating that it supports the creation of pathways that allow an attacker to move from a lower-privilege state to a higher-privilege state. The technique can be used to establish a persistent presence on the target, enabling long-term access and control. It is often employed in post-exploitation phases, where the goal is to expand access within a compromised network. The relationship between the executable upload webshell and privilege escalation is bidirectional: the webshell enables the path, and the path enables the full exploitation potential of the webshell. This technique is commonly used in advanced persistent threat (APT) scenarios and is a critical component in the lateral movement and privilege escalation stages of cyberattacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">requires, supports, establishes, supports testing for, enables, can establish</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ffd8f37d7d75ed447c448d9b518f200d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b0ebb35df72c979d0b12d18b62e291d3-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002</data>
