<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Uploaded Webshell">
  <data key="d8">17.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Executable Upload Webshell-Uploaded Webshell is a technique that results in the creation of an uploaded webshell artifact. This process involves the deployment of malicious code onto a web server, typically through a file upload mechanism, allowing an attacker to gain unauthorized access and control over the system. The technique produces an uploaded webshell as a direct outcome, which functions as a backdoor for ongoing exploitation. The resulting artifact is a webshell that has been successfully uploaded to the target environment, enabling remote command execution and persistent access. The uploaded webshell artifact may take various forms, such as PHP, ASP, or JSP files, depending on the server's configuration and the attacker's objectives. The technique is commonly used in cyberattacks to establish a foothold within a compromised system, often as part of broader intrusion campaigns. The produced artifact is characterized by its ability to execute arbitrary commands via a web interface, making it a significant threat in web application security. The technique can be triggered through vulnerable file upload functionalities, where insufficient input validation allows the malicious file to be uploaded and executed. The resulting uploaded webshell artifact is typically stored on the server and can be accessed through a web browser, allowing the attacker to interact with the system remotely. The process is often automated or facilitated by scripts that exploit known vulnerabilities in web applications. The technique is closely associated with web shell attacks and is frequently observed in real-world cyber incidents involving web application compromise.</data>
  <data key="d10">can produce, produces</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-002</data>
