<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Password Hash">
  <data key="d8">9.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (Executable Upload Webshell, Password Hash) involves the interaction between the technique of executable upload via a webshell and the generation or consumption of password hashes. This technique can produce password hash artifacts as a result of its execution, with multiple descriptions confirming that it may generate one or more password hashes as an output. The produced password hash is explicitly noted as an artifact, indicating that it is a byproduct or result of the process. Additionally, some descriptions indicate that the technique can consume password hashes, suggesting a dual capability—both producing and utilizing password hashes in its operation. The consistent mention of password hash artifacts across multiple descriptions highlights their significance as a key output. While the descriptions vary slightly in phrasing, they collectively emphasize that the (Executable Upload Webshell, Password Hash) relation is associated with the creation and potential use of password hash artifacts, with no conflicting information regarding the nature of the relation.</data>
