<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="HTTP Redirect Or Cookie">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The technique known as (Executable Upload Webshell, HTTP Redirect Or Cookie) is indicated by the presence of an HTTP redirect or a change in cookies, which serve as signals of its success. These indicators—either an HTTP redirect or a cookie change—can be observed following the execution of the technique and are used to confirm that the webshell upload has been completed successfully. The technique may produce HTTP redirects or cookies as observable artifacts, and their occurrence or alteration is interpreted as evidence of the technique's successful deployment. The presence of a redirect or a cookie change is consistently cited across descriptions as a reliable indicator of the technique’s success, with variations in phrasing emphasizing either the redirect or the cookie as the signaling mechanism. In all cases, the change or presence of either an HTTP redirect or a cookie is directly tied to the outcome of the webshell upload process.</data>
  <data key="d10">indicated by,indicates,produces</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
