<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="Protocol Allowlist">
  <data key="d8">13.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Executable Upload Webshell-Protocol Allowlist is a cybersecurity technique that enables an attacker to bypass protocol allowlist controls by uploading an executable webshell. This method exploits the restriction mechanisms designed to permit only specific, authorized protocols, allowing unauthorized code execution through the upload of malicious scripts. The protocol allowlist defensive control is intended to block such attempts by restricting the types of protocols that can be used, thereby mitigating the risk of executable upload webshell attacks. However, the technique can circumvent this control, effectively bypassing the protocol allowlist. While the control is designed to defend against the executable upload webshell technique by limiting allowed protocols, it may be compromised if the attack successfully evades these restrictions. The technique may be blocked by the protocol allowlist defensive control, but it also has the capability to bypass such controls, indicating a potential vulnerability in the enforcement mechanism. The control is effective in blocking the technique by restricting allowed protocols, but its efficacy depends on the implementation and the sophistication of the attack. In some cases, the control may be bypassed by the technique, highlighting the ongoing challenge of maintaining secure protocol enforcement. The Executable Upload Webshell-Protocol Allowlist technique represents a known exploit path that adversaries may use to compromise systems despite the presence of protocol allowlist defenses.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks, defends against, bypasses, mitigates, blocked by</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d12">source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-463bc40b9d3a7e65.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f0615c6655a21111.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-0d4e246da395857e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-370982d0d06e0982.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md</data>
