<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="WAF Or Request Filter">
  <data key="d8">14.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Executable Upload Webshell-WAF Or Request Filter is a cybersecurity relation that describes the interaction between a defensive control and a malicious technique. The technique, known as executable upload webshell, involves an attacker uploading a malicious script (webshell) to a web server, typically to gain unauthorized access or execute commands remotely. The defensive control, referred to as a WAF (Web Application Firewall) or request filter, is designed to detect and block such malicious uploads by analyzing incoming requests. This control mitigates executable upload webshell attempts by filtering requests for suspicious patterns, such as executable file types or malicious payloads, and blocks them before they can be processed. The control defends against the technique by identifying and blocking malicious requests, thereby preventing the upload of webshells. However, the technique may bypass the WAF or request filter defensive control, either through obfuscation, encoding, or other evasion methods. Some descriptions indicate that the control can be bypassed by the technique, suggesting that while the control is effective in many cases, it is not foolproof. In certain scenarios, the technique may successfully evade detection and upload a webshell despite the presence of the control. The control may block the technique by filtering requests, but the effectiveness depends on the sophistication of both the attack and the defensive mechanism. Overall, the relation highlights a continuous cat-and-mouse dynamic between attackers attempting to bypass security controls and defenders aiming to prevent unauthorized uploads.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks, defends against, may be blocked by, may bypass, bypasses, mitigates, blocked by</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000</data>
