<edge source="Executable Upload Webshell" target="URL Userinfo Confusion Payload">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Executable Upload Webshell-URL Userinfo Confusion Payload is a specific payload pattern utilized within the executable upload webshell technique. This technique involves uploading malicious executable files to a web server to gain unauthorized access or control. The payload leverages the URL userinfo confusion method, which exploits the way certain web servers parse and process URLs containing userinfo components (typically in the format `http://username:password@host/path`). By embedding malicious code or commands within the userinfo section of a URL, attackers can bypass security mechanisms that fail to properly sanitize or validate such inputs. This payload pattern is specifically designed to be used in conjunction with the executable upload webshell technique, where it may be delivered through crafted URLs to initiate or facilitate the upload of malicious executables. The payload is not a standalone exploit but rather a component that enhances the effectiveness of the webshell technique by enabling covert command delivery or execution. The technique relies on the payload pattern to manipulate server-side processing, often exploiting misconfigurations or vulnerabilities in URL parsing routines. The use of this payload is consistent across various implementations of the executable upload webshell method, indicating its role as a recognized tactic in web-based attacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, used by, used in</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
