<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Escalate Privileges">
  <data key="d8">29.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation Escalate Privileges-JWT Token Forgery describes a connection between the technique of JWT Token Forgery and the attack goal of escalating privileges. JWT Token Forgery is a technique that enables an attacker to manipulate or forge JSON Web Tokens, which are commonly used for authentication and authorization in web applications. By forging a valid JWT token, an attacker can impersonate a legitimate user or gain access to resources beyond their authorized permissions. This technique directly supports the goal of escalating privileges, as it allows the attacker to achieve higher access levels within a system. The technique can be used to gain elevated privileges by exploiting weaknesses in token validation mechanisms, such as improper signature verification or the use of weak secret keys. It supports the achievement of the goal of privilege escalation by enabling unauthorized access to privileged functions or data. The relation also indicates that this technique can be employed during security testing to assess the resilience of authentication systems against such attacks. Overall, JWT Token Forgery is a critical method for achieving privilege escalation, and its use is closely tied to the successful execution of the attack goal Escalate Privileges.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, can support, supports testing for, supports attack goal, achieves, supports achieving</data>
