<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Internal Service Reachability">
  <data key="d8">13.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Internal Service Reachability-JWT Token Forgery refers to a cybersecurity technique that leverages the ability to access internal services within a network to facilitate JWT (JSON Web Token) token forgery. This technique fundamentally depends on internal service reachability, which is both a prerequisite and a supporting capability. The attacker must possess the capability to interact with backend systems, as internal service reachability enables such interactions. Without this reachability, the technique cannot be executed. The technique not only requires internal service reachability but also supports its establishment as an attacker capability, allowing the adversary to achieve the necessary access to internal services. This capability is essential for exploiting vulnerabilities that allow the forging of JWT tokens, often by manipulating authentication mechanisms or exploiting misconfigurations in service-to-service communication. The technique is inherently tied to the ability to reach internal services, making this reachability a core requirement and a key enabler for the attack.</data>
  <data key="d10">requires, supports, supports achieving, enables, can establish</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000</data>
