<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Config File">
  <data key="d8">13.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Config File-JWT Token Forgery refers to a relationship where the JWT token forgery technique generates a config file as an artifact. This technique is capable of producing config files, which are created as a byproduct of the forgery process. The config file artifact is directly produced by the JWT token forgery technique, and multiple descriptions confirm that the technique can generate such files. The artifact may take the form of a single config file or multiple config files, depending on the execution context. The production of the config file is a consistent outcome of the technique, indicating that the creation of this file is an integral part of the forgery process. While the descriptions vary slightly in phrasing, they all converge on the same core idea: the JWT token forgery technique results in the creation of a config file artifact.</data>
  <data key="d10">produced, can produce, produces</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4fe7170e2d9c9211e7f5a9c957dd660-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9ddc793324d868b5ed0d90f4c192307-chunk-000</data>
