<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="WAF Or Request Filter">
  <data key="d8">13.0</data>
  <data key="d9">JWT Token Forgery-WAF Or Request Filter refers to a cybersecurity technique involving the manipulation or creation of forged JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) to bypass security controls such as Web Application Firewalls (WAFs) or request filters. This technique enables attackers to exploit vulnerabilities in authentication mechanisms by submitting maliciously crafted JWTs, potentially gaining unauthorized access to systems or resources. The primary goal of the technique is to circumvent protective measures designed to detect and block such forged tokens. Defensive controls, including WAFs and request filters, are implemented to mitigate JWT token forgery attempts by analyzing incoming requests for suspicious patterns, malformed tokens, or unauthorized claims. These controls block the technique by filtering malicious requests, identifying forged tokens based on signature validation, expiration checks, or issuer verification, and preventing their processing. While the technique may be blocked by these defensive mechanisms, its effectiveness depends on the sophistication of the forgery and the robustness of the filtering logic. Some controls are specifically configured to detect and block the act of JWT token forgery, while others may only partially mitigate the threat, depending on the implementation. In certain cases, the technique may still succeed if the WAF or request filter fails to recognize the forged token due to incomplete rule sets or evasion techniques. Overall, the interaction between JWT token forgery and WAF or request filter controls highlights the ongoing challenge of balancing security efficacy with the need to allow legitimate authentication flows.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique can bypass WAF or request filter defenses.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks,bypasses,may be blocked by,mitigates</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
