<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Move Laterally">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">JWT Token Forgery, Move Laterally is a technique that supports the goal of moving laterally within a network environment. This technique involves the manipulation or creation of JWT (JSON Web Tokens) to gain unauthorized access to systems or resources, thereby enabling an attacker to extend their presence across the network. By forging valid JWT tokens, an attacker can impersonate legitimate users or services, bypassing authentication mechanisms and exploiting trust relationships. The technique is specifically designed to facilitate lateral movement, allowing the attacker to navigate from an initially compromised system to other systems within the same network. This capability is critical in advanced persistent threat (APT) scenarios where attackers aim to escalate privileges and maintain persistence. The technique can support the attack goal of moving laterally by leveraging weaknesses in token validation processes, such as weak secret keys, improper signature verification, or insecure token storage. It is often employed in scenarios where attackers have already obtained initial access and seek to expand their control. The effectiveness of JWT Token Forgery depends on the security posture of the target environment, particularly how JWTs are issued, validated, and protected. When properly implemented, JWT validation mechanisms can prevent such attacks, but vulnerabilities in these processes can be exploited to enable lateral movement. The technique is commonly associated with web applications and APIs that use JWTs for authentication and authorization.</data>
  <data key="d10">can support,supports,supports achieving</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-000</data>
