<edge source="JWT Token Forgery" target="Obtain Account Access">
  <data key="d8">9.0</data>
  <data key="d9">JWT Token Forgery, Obtain Account Access is a technique that supports the goal of obtaining account access. This method involves the manipulation or creation of JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) to gain unauthorized access to user accounts. The technique can be used to bypass authentication mechanisms by forging valid JWTs, thereby enabling attackers to impersonate legitimate users. It supports achieving the goal of obtaining account access by exploiting vulnerabilities in token generation, validation, or storage processes. The technique may also be employed during security testing to evaluate the resilience of systems against such attacks. While the primary purpose of JWT Token Forgery is to achieve account access, it is also used in the context of penetration testing to assess the security posture of applications. The technique directly contributes to the goal of obtaining account access, and its effectiveness depends on weaknesses in the implementation of JWT-based authentication systems. In some cases, the technique may involve exploiting misconfigurations, weak secret keys, or improper signature validation. Overall, JWT Token Forgery is a recognized method for achieving the objective of obtaining account access, and its use highlights the importance of secure JWT handling practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique supports obtaining account access by forging tokens.</data>
