<edge source="Escalate Privileges" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">35.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Escalate Privileges-SQL Injection File Read is a technique that supports the goal of escalating privileges within a system. This method leverages SQL injection vulnerabilities to gain elevated access rights, enabling an attacker to perform actions beyond their initial user permissions. The technique is specifically aligned with the attack goal of privilege escalation, and it can be used to achieve this objective by exploiting weaknesses in database query handling. It supports both the direct and indirect achievement of privilege escalation, often through the manipulation of SQL queries to extract or modify data in ways that reveal or grant administrative-level access. The technique may also be employed during security testing to identify and assess the risk of privilege escalation via SQL injection. In some contexts, it is used to test for the presence of such vulnerabilities, reinforcing its role in both offensive and defensive cybersecurity practices. The technique is consistently described as a means to achieve or support the broader attack goal of escalating privileges, with multiple descriptions emphasizing its utility in enabling unauthorized access and control.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, can support, supports testing for, achieves, supports achieving</data>
