<edge source="Read Sensitive Data" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">25.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Read Sensitive Data-SQL Injection File Read is a technique that supports the attack goal of reading sensitive data. This technique leverages SQL injection vulnerabilities to gain unauthorized access to files on a system, enabling the extraction of sensitive information such as configuration files, credentials, or other confidential data. By exploiting improper input validation in SQL queries, an attacker can manipulate database queries to execute commands that read files from the server's file system. The technique is specifically associated with the broader objective of reading sensitive data, and it can be used both to achieve this goal and to test for the presence of such vulnerabilities. It is often employed in penetration testing and ethical hacking scenarios to assess system security. The technique is closely tied to the attack goal "Read Sensitive Data," and multiple descriptions confirm its role in supporting this objective. In some contexts, it is explicitly referred to as "SQL Injection File Read," highlighting the method's focus on file access via SQL injection. The consistency across descriptions underscores its established relevance in cybersecurity frameworks for identifying and exploiting data exposure risks.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, supports achieving, can support, supports testing for</data>
