<edge source="Execute Code" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">10.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (Execute Code, SQL Injection File Read) refers to a technique that supports the attack goal of executing code. This technique is specifically associated with SQL injection vulnerabilities, where malicious input is injected into a database query to manipulate the system. By exploiting such vulnerabilities, an attacker can leverage the SQL injection mechanism to execute arbitrary code on the target system. The technique enables the execution of code by manipulating the database's query processing, potentially allowing the attacker to read files from the server's file system, execute commands, or gain unauthorized access. This capability is critical in advancing an attack, as it allows the attacker to move beyond data extraction and achieve full control over the system. The relation highlights the connection between SQL injection and the broader objective of code execution, emphasizing that file reading in this context is often a means to achieve or facilitate code execution. The technique is commonly used in scenarios where the attacker aims to escalate privileges, retrieve sensitive data, or establish persistent access. While the primary focus is on code execution, the ability to read files can provide necessary information or payloads to support this goal. This relation underscores the importance of securing database inputs and preventing SQL injection to mitigate the risk of unauthorized code execution.&lt;SEP&gt;The goal supports achieving the goal of executing code.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique supports achieving the goal of executing code.</data>
