<edge source="Boolean Response Delta" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">10.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (Boolean Response Delta, SQL Injection File Read) refers to a technique used in the context of SQL injection attacks where the success of the attack is determined by analyzing a boolean response delta. This delta represents a change in the system's response—typically a difference in output, such as a page loading differently or a status change—when a malicious SQL query is executed. The technique relies on observing whether the response to a query yields a true or false outcome, which is reflected in the response delta. A boolean response delta, therefore, serves as an indicator of the technique’s success, with a detectable change in response signaling that the injection was effective. The consistency across multiple descriptions emphasizes that the presence of a boolean response delta is a reliable marker for confirming the success of the SQL injection attempt. This method is commonly used in automated testing or exploitation scenarios where the attacker seeks to infer data or gain unauthorized access through database queries.&lt;SEP&gt;Boolean Response Delta can indicate the result of SQL Injection File Read.&lt;SEP&gt;A boolean response delta indicates the technique's success.</data>
