<edge source="Credential Exposure" target="SSRF Localhost Probing">
  <data key="d8">16.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Credential Exposure-SSRF Localhost Probing is a technique that targets and exploits vulnerabilities related to credential exposure, particularly within the context of Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks involving localhost probing. This method is designed to test for and exploit weaknesses where sensitive credentials may be inadvertently exposed through misconfigured services or applications accessible via localhost. The technique specifically leverages SSRF vulnerabilities to probe local network endpoints, potentially revealing credentials stored in configuration files, environment variables, or internal APIs. It is used to assess the security posture of systems by identifying whether credential exposure exists due to improper access controls or insecure service configurations. The technique may exploit credential exposure either directly or indirectly, depending on the target environment and the availability of accessible endpoints. It supports both testing and exploitation phases, enabling security researchers and attackers alike to detect and potentially leverage exposed credentials. The vulnerability class of credential exposure is directly exploited by this technique, which operates by sending crafted requests to localhost or internal services to retrieve sensitive information. While the primary focus is on identifying and exploiting credential exposure, the technique may also reveal broader security misconfigurations. Conflicts in descriptions are minimal, as all statements align around the core function: exploiting credential exposure through SSRF-based localhost probing. The technique is consistently described as targeting, testing, or exploiting credential exposure, with no indication of distinct entities or conflicting interpretations.</data>
  <data key="d10">may exploit, supports testing for, exploits, tests or exploits, targets</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
