<edge source="Credential Exposure" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">10.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation (Credential Exposure, SQL Injection File Read) refers to a technique that leverages SQL injection to exploit vulnerabilities related to credential exposure. This technique is used to test or exploit the vulnerability class known as Credential Exposure, which involves the unintended exposure of sensitive authentication credentials. The method specifically targets weaknesses where credentials are accessible or retrievable due to insecure system configurations or flawed code practices. By exploiting SQL injection, the technique enables unauthorized access to files or data that may contain exposed credentials, thereby demonstrating or enabling the exploitation of credential exposure vulnerabilities. The technique supports testing for the weakness class where credentials are exposed, often through file read operations enabled by SQL injection flaws. It is primarily used to identify and exploit scenarios in which credentials are stored insecurely or are accessible via path traversal or file inclusion vulnerabilities. The relation highlights the intersection between SQL injection and credential exposure, emphasizing that SQL injection can serve as a vector to access or extract sensitive credential information. This connection underscores the importance of securing database inputs and preventing file read operations through proper input validation and access controls.</data>
  <data key="d10">exploits,supports testing for,tests or exploits</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2c01c9361375f50dd8673c9eb15cacd0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
