<edge source="URL Userinfo Confusion Payload" target="SQL Injection File Read">
  <data key="d8">30.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SQL Injection File Read-URL Userinfo Confusion Payload is a technique employed in SQL injection attacks to read files from a target system by exploiting the URL userinfo confusion payload pattern. This payload pattern is specifically utilized within the context of SQL injection file read techniques, enabling attackers to leverage the parsing behavior of certain web servers or applications that misinterpret the userinfo component of a URL. The technique relies on the fact that some systems incorrectly process the userinfo section (the part of a URL between the '://' and the '@' symbol) as part of the path or query, allowing malicious input to be injected into the SQL query context. By crafting a URL with a specially formatted userinfo component, attackers can trigger SQL injection vulnerabilities that result in the extraction of sensitive files from the server. The payload pattern supports and facilitates this file read behavior, making it a recognized method in the exploitation of SQL injection flaws. The technique is consistently described as using the URL userinfo confusion payload pattern, with variations in phrasing across descriptions emphasizing either the payload's function, its role in exploitation, or its integration into the broader file read attack strategy. The pattern is not limited to a single implementation but is recognized as a consistent method across multiple attack scenarios involving SQL injection and file access.</data>
  <data key="d10">supports, uses, used by, targets, used in</data>
