<edge source="URL Userinfo Confusion Payload" target="Protocol Allowlist">
  <data key="d8">14.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Protocol Allowlist-URL Userinfo Confusion Payload refers to a specific type of exploit payload designed to bypass protocol allowlist controls by leveraging confusion in the URL userinfo component. This payload pattern exploits the way certain systems parse and interpret URL structures, particularly focusing on the userinfo section (the part of a URL that typically contains username and password information, such as `user:pass@domain`). By manipulating the userinfo field in a crafted URL, the payload can evade detection mechanisms that rely on protocol allowlist enforcement, which is intended to restrict access to only permitted protocols (e.g., HTTP, HTTPS). The payload may bypass these controls because the parsing logic fails to correctly identify or block malicious constructs embedded within the userinfo portion, allowing unauthorized or potentially harmful protocols to be executed or processed. While the control mechanism is designed to block such payloads—especially those exploiting URL userinfo confusion—this specific payload pattern can circumvent the enforcement under certain conditions. The effectiveness of the bypass depends on the implementation of the allowlist and the parsing behavior of the target system. In some cases, the control may successfully block the payload, but in others, the exploit remains effective due to parsing inconsistencies or insufficient validation. The payload may be used in security testing or malicious attacks to test or exploit systems that enforce protocol allowlists without fully accounting for edge cases in URL parsing.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks, bypasses, can bypass</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-429f1cea7765f3e2.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-d1ffa3e33fee59c7.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-045067d746e8d66c.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67281ef7361eaa1e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-db59b660c03f0d7d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md</data>
  <data key="d13">1787992127</data>
