  <data key="d15">Protocol Allowlist</data>
  <data key="d16">URL Userinfo Confusion Payload</data>
</edge>
<edge source="URL Userinfo Confusion Payload" target="SSRF Localhost Probing">
  <data key="d8">16.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SSRF Localhost Probing-URL Userinfo Confusion Payload is a specific payload pattern utilized in Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks, particularly in techniques designed to probe localhost services. This payload leverages the URL userinfo confusion mechanism, where the userinfo component of a URL (typically used for authentication credentials) is manipulated to bypass security filters or trigger unintended behavior in web applications. The payload pattern is employed by SSRF localhost probing techniques to exploit misconfigurations or vulnerabilities in URL parsing logic, enabling attackers to test or access internal network resources. It is specifically designed to target the behavior associated with SSRF localhost probing, where the goal is to determine the accessibility of internal services from a vulnerable application. The technique relies on the confusion between the userinfo field and other parts of the URL structure, allowing the payload to be interpreted in unintended ways. This payload pattern is consistently used across various SSRF probing methods to exploit vulnerabilities in how URLs are processed, especially when input validation is inadequate. The payload is not limited to a single implementation but is a recognized pattern within the broader context of SSRF attack vectors, often used to bypass security mechanisms that fail to properly validate or sanitize URL components.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, used by, used in</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5e4ee546aa8f7ecfb659ca7fb68e9be9-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4a49f72fdeac26b85fd80fd22bf2c4b9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-da0c7cc16e444f7a837833f0b1605208-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8ad4036a778fcc22e1513e5f0c0a8591-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-045067d746e8d66c.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-516d729c800024a5.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-db59b660c03f0d7d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-a9ccf5fa80acec79.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-2e266fadcba1fc0d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-f185a95c8594da55.md</data>
  <data key="d13">1787992447</data>
