<edge source="SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload" target="WAF Or Request Filter">
  <data key="d8">10.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload-WAF Or Request Filter is a payload pattern designed to circumvent web application firewalls (WAFs) or request filtering mechanisms. This payload exploits weaknesses in security controls that are intended to block unauthorized or malicious input, particularly those related to SQL injection attacks. The pattern enables the bypass of WAF or request filter controls by leveraging SQL comment syntax to obscure or manipulate authentication-related logic. While the control is designed to block such payloads when properly enforced, the payload can successfully evade detection and enforcement under certain conditions. In some configurations, the control may fail to detect or block the SQL comment auth bypass payload, allowing it to pass through undetected. Conversely, when the WAF or request filter is properly configured and active, the control can effectively block the payload. The effectiveness of the bypass depends on the specific implementation and sensitivity of the filtering rules. The payload's ability to bypass these controls highlights potential vulnerabilities in security systems that rely on signature-based or pattern-matching detection for SQL injection defense.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks, bypasses, can bypass</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-429f1cea7765f3e2.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-d1ffa3e33fee59c7.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md</data>
  <data key="d13">1787992203</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
  <data key="d15">SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload</data>
