<edge source="SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload" target="SSRF Localhost Probing">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload-SSRF Localhost Probing is a technique that leverages a specific payload pattern to exploit Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerabilities, particularly in scenarios involving localhost probing. The payload, known as the SQL comment auth bypass payload, is designed to bypass authentication mechanisms by injecting SQL comment syntax, allowing unauthorized access to internal systems. This payload pattern is specifically used in SSRF localhost probing, where the goal is to probe internal network services that are only accessible from the local machine. The technique targets the use of SQL comment auth bypass payloads to exploit misconfigurations or insecure input validation in web applications. It is employed in SSRF probing techniques to test or exploit internal endpoints, often using the payload to manipulate request behavior and gain insight into internal network structures. The payload pattern is integral to the SSRF localhost probing technique, enabling attackers to bypass security controls and probe internal resources. While the technique primarily focuses on exploiting SSRF vulnerabilities, it also involves the use of SQL comment syntax to bypass authentication, highlighting a convergence of SQL injection and SSRF attack vectors. The payload is consistently applied in the context of SSRF localhost probing, making it a key component in reconnaissance and exploitation phases of such attacks.</data>
  <data key="d10">targets, uses, used in</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1460b2cac00bc568a22b020dc995d48d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8c971a08d484b9763ebcf9e596a7147e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca4ebbe397b88a5e1985154047a1fd42-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-02d8de5bc4d7ef5b5730e6de21983a27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ea557e757697285d.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67d16a04c4799edd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-16c3d9d4e9cc3637.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67281ef7361eaa1e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-4dbc50aa9b3261a0.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-bae40e62361a8519.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-7e31c39a962ccdd6.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-a9ccf5fa80acec79.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-eae76c910437f664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-ec1ac76eae51358e.md</data>
  <data key="d13">1787991755</data>
