  <data key="d16">SSRF Localhost Probing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload" target="Protocol Allowlist">
  <data key="d8">8.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The (Protocol Allowlist, SQL Comment Auth Bypass Payload) refers to a specific payload pattern designed to circumvent protocol allowlist controls, which are security mechanisms intended to restrict interactions to predefined, authorized protocols. This payload exploits a vulnerability by leveraging SQL comment syntax to bypass the enforcement of protocol allowlists, allowing unauthorized or unintended protocol usage. The payload pattern can effectively evade detection and enforcement mechanisms that rely on filtering or validating protocol types. In some cases, the payload bypasses protocol allowlist controls entirely, enabling access or execution that would otherwise be blocked. However, when a protocol allowlist is properly enforced, the control can block the payload, indicating that the effectiveness of the bypass depends on the configuration and implementation of the allowlist mechanism. The payload is specifically associated with SQL comment-based techniques, which are commonly used in authentication bypass attacks. This suggests that the payload may be used in contexts where SQL injection or related injection vulnerabilities are present, allowing attackers to manipulate authentication logic by inserting comments that disrupt expected protocol validation. The consistency of the description across multiple sources confirms that the payload is recognized as a method to bypass protocol allowlist controls, though its success is contingent upon the security posture of the system in question.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks,bypasses</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-774dd7b69cee60333fe159b91c5115dc-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0584c585862d9a9383e3c2512964e051-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-becce52057339c535889e197f6df8c45-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e8b98451fa828a77a410acce1592cf2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8261eb5533257b5d5534c19022f92a0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f480ea9fcbb09d97e0819addf2df923b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d12">source-1bcb83f8254416e4.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-429f1cea7765f3e2.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-d1ffa3e33fee59c7.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-3f0581573d61b7bd.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-67281ef7361eaa1e.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-12ff71155a138664.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-829d6e7cad18eac1.md&lt;SEP&gt;source-edb2f8f9e3bad28b.md</data>
