<edge source="Protocol Allowlist" target="SSRF Localhost Probing">
  <data key="d8">16.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Protocol Allowlist-SSRF Localhost Probing technique refers to a method used in security testing and exploitation where an attacker attempts to bypass a protocol allowlist control by leveraging Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) to probe localhost addresses. This technique exploits the configuration of protocol allowlists, which are designed to restrict outgoing network requests to specific protocols (e.g., HTTP, HTTPS, FTP) to prevent unauthorized access. By crafting SSRF requests that target localhost or internal network endpoints, attackers may circumvent these restrictions, enabling access to internal services that are not exposed externally. The protocol allowlist control is intended to block such attempts, and in some configurations, it successfully mitigates SSRF localhost probing by rejecting requests that use disallowed protocols or target internal IP ranges. However, the technique can bypass the allowlist when the control is improperly configured or when the attacker exploits edge cases, such as using alternative protocol schemes or encoding methods that evade detection. In certain scenarios, the allowlist may be ineffective due to misconfigurations, lack of comprehensive protocol validation, or insufficient filtering of internal network traffic. Thus, while the protocol allowlist is a defensive mechanism designed to block the SSRF localhost probing technique, its effectiveness depends on implementation rigor. The technique may be blocked by a properly configured allowlist, but it can also bypass such controls, particularly when the allowlist fails to account for all possible attack vectors or when the attacker leverages protocol-level bypasses.</data>
  <data key="d10">blocks, may be blocked by, may bypass, bypasses, mitigates</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-67f151b5c1ed66e0d6be294a338e261a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20d020c04f02649ff62131f95e1cf5af-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20e319f206fb018ed527c5b31c09ddf0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4689e3344d4cedcec51062aefaf0b4c4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92c7622093c392d46fd0e476d89c0395-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1a922685f9944c8d348cfa4732a95f15-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c8df9b099194a66605da7b496d31a4a5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b7c72285e15bcd2791980b58faff89f6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6a368a385f7056f3a4e83a6daacc92e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b9fbca654baa1f52872a4a45acdf6ffb-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-880110b45de32b68e00014bf0300aced-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3e8a9899a4d34db71efbd953d99c628b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c4f1b727935e166da3087ad74c41475b-chunk-000</data>
